用","AIモデルの推論とサービスをサポート","Ascendハードウェアプラットフォームに対応","オープンソース且つカスタマイズ可能"],"ko":["커뮤니티 유지 보수 하드웨어 플러그인","vLLM의 Ascend에서의 추론 및 서비스에 사용","AI 모델 추론 및 서비스를 지원","Ascend 하드웨어 플랫폼에 대응","오픈 소스且고 커스터마이즈 가능"],"es":["Compatibilidad con vLLM en Ascend","Inferencia en hardware Ascend","Servicio de modelos de código abierto","Diseñado para la comunidad de desarrolladores","Soporte para la inferencia en tiempo real"],"fr":["Compatibilité avec vLLM sur Ascend","Inférence sur le matériel Ascend","Service de modèles open source","Conçu pour la communauté des développeurs","Prise en charge de l''inférence en temps réel"],"de":["Kompatibilität mit vLLM auf Ascend","Inferenz auf Ascend-Hardware","Open-Source-Modell-Service","Entwickelt für die Entwicklergemeinschaft","Unterstützung für Echtzeit-Inferenz"],"pt":["Integração nativa entre vLLM e hardware Ascend NPU","Otimizado para serving de modelos Transformer de grande escala","Suporte para inferência de LLMs de baixa latência e alta throughput","Mantido pela comunidade de código aberto","Compatível com operações padrão de LLMops e MLOps"],"ru":["Нативная интеграция между vLLM и аппаратным обеспечением Ascend NPU","Оптимизирован для обслуживания крупномасштабных моделей Transformer","Поддержка низкозатратного вывода LLM с высокой пропускной способностью","Поддерживается сообществом с открытым исходным кодом","Совместим со стандартными операциями LLMops и MLOps"],"ar":["تكامل أصلي بين vLLM وأجهزة Ascend NPU","مُحسّن لتقديم نماذج Transformer واسعة النطاق","دعم استدلال LLM منخفض الكمون وذو إنتاجية عالية","مُدار من قبل المجتمع مفتوح المصدر","متوافق مع عمليات LLMops و MLOps القياسية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","vLLM Ascend","硬件插件","AI模型推理","如何使用vllm-ascend-model-adapter","vllm-ascend-model-adapter安装指南","vllm-ascend-model-adapter替代品"],"ja":["AIエージェント","vLLM Ascend","ハードウェアプラグイン","AIモデルの推論","vllm-ascend-model-adapterの使い方","vllm-ascend-model-adapterのインストールガイド","vllm-ascend-model-adapterの代替品"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","vLLM Ascend","하드웨어 플러그인","AI 모델 추론","vllm-ascend-model-adapter 사용법","vllm-ascend-model-adapter 설치 가이드","vllm-ascend-model-adapter 대체품"],"es":["cómo usar vllm-ascend-model-adapter","qué es vLLM","alternativas a vllm-ascend-model-adapter","vllm-ascend-model-adapter vs otros modelos","instalación de vllm-ascend-model-adapter","guía de configuración de vllm-ascend-model-adapter","desarrollo de modelos de IA con vllm-ascend-model-adapter"],"fr":["comment utiliser vllm-ascend-model-adapter","quoi est vLLM","alternatives à vllm-ascend-model-adapter","vllm-ascend-model-adapter vs autres modèles","installation de vllm-ascend-model-adapter","guide de configuration de vllm-ascend-model-adapter","développement de modèles d''IA avec vllm-ascend-model-adapter"],"de":["wie man vllm-ascend-model-adapter verwendet","was ist vLLM","Alternativen zu vllm-ascend-model-adapter","vllm-ascend-model-adapter vs andere Modelle","Installation von vllm-ascend-model-adapter","Konfigurationsanleitung für vllm-ascend-model-adapter","Entwicklung von KI-Modellen mit vllm-ascend-model-adapter"],"pt":["vllm ascend adapter","como usar vllm no ascend","inferência llm ascend","vllm vs tensorrt","instalar vllm ascend","llmops hardware ascend","model serving ascend","otimização transformer ascend"],"ru":["адаптер vllm для ascend","как использовать vllm на ascend","вывод llm на ascend","vllm vs tensorrt","установить vllm ascend","llmops оборудование ascend","обслуживание моделей ascend","оптимизация transformer ascend"],"ar":["محول vllm لـ ascend","كيفية استخدام vllm على ascend","استدلال llm على ascend","vllm مقابل tensorrt","تثبيت vllm ascend","أجهزة llmops ascend","تقديم النماذج ascend","تحسين transformer ascend"]}},"owner":"vllm-project","repo":"vllm-ascend","repoPath":"vllm-project/vllm-ascend","stars":1712,"forks":860,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T14:54:04Z","topics":["ascend","inference","llm","llm-serving","llmops","mlops","model-serving","transformer","vllm"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vllm-ascend-model-adapter","description":"Adapt and debug existing or new models for vLLM on Ascend NPU. Implement in /vllm-workspace/vllm and /vllm-workspace/vllm-ascend, validate via direct vllm serve from /workspace, and deliver one signed commit in the current repo.","bodyPreview":"# vLLM Ascend Model Adapter\n\n## Overview\n\nAdapt Hugging Face or local models to run on `vllm-ascend` with minimal changes, deterministic validation, and single-commit delivery. This skill is for both already-supported models and new architectures not yet registered in vLLM.\n\n## Read order\n\n1. Start with `references/workflow-checklist.md`.\n2. Read `references/multimodal-ep-aclgraph-lessons.md` (feature-first checklist).\n3. If startup/inference fails, read `references/troubleshooting.md`.\n4. If ch","body":"# vLLM Ascend Model Adapter\n\n## Overview\n\nAdapt Hugging Face or local models to run on `vllm-ascend` with minimal changes, deterministic validation, and single-commit delivery. This skill is for both already-supported models and new architectures not yet registered in vLLM.\n\n## Read order\n\n1. Start with `references/workflow-checklist.md`.\n2. Read `references/multimodal-ep-aclgraph-lessons.md` (feature-first checklist).\n3. If startup/inference fails, read `references/troubleshooting.md`.\n4. If checkpoint is fp8-on-NPU, read `references/fp8-on-npu-lessons.md`.\n5. Before handoff, read `references/deliverables.md`.\n\n## Hard constraints\n\n- Never upgrade `transformers`.\n- Primary implementation roots are fixed by Dockerfile:\n    - `/vllm-workspace/vllm`\n    - `/vllm-workspace/vllm-ascend`\n- Start `vllm serve` from `/workspace` with direct command by default.\n- Default API port is `8000` unless user explicitly asks otherwise.\n- Feature-first default: try best to validate ACLGraph / EP / flashcomm1 / MTP / multimodal out-of-box.\n- `--enable-expert-parallel` and flashcomm1 checks are MoE-only; for non-MoE models mark as not-applicable with evidence.\n- If any feature cannot be enabled, keep evidence and explain reason in final report.\n- Do not rely on `PYTHONPATH=<modified-src>:$PYTHONPATH` unless debugging fallback is strictly needed.\n- Keep code changes minimal and focused on the target model.\n- Final deliverable commit must be one single signed commit in the current working repo (`git commit -sm ...`).\n- Keep final docs in Chinese and compact.\n- **Dummy-first is encouraged for speed, but dummy is NOT fully equivalent to real weights.**\n- **Never sign off adaptation using dummy-only evidence; real-weight gate is mandatory.**\n\n## Execution playbook\n\n### 1) Collect context\n\n- Confirm model path (default `/models/<model-name>`; if environment differs, confirm with user explicitly).\n- Confirm implementation roots (`/vllm-workspace/vllm`, `/vllm-workspace/vllm-ascend`).\n- Confirm delivery root (the current git repo where the final commit is expected).\n- Confirm runtime import path points to `/vllm-workspace/*` install.\n- Use default expected feature set: ACLGraph + EP + flashcomm1 + MTP + multimodal (if model has VL capability).\n- User requirements extend this baseline, not replace it.\n\n### 2) Analyze model first\n\n- Inspect `config.json`, processor files, modeling files, tokenizer files.\n- Identify architecture class, attention variant, quantization type, and multimodal requirements.\n- Check state-dict key prefixes (and safetensors index) to infer mapping needs.\n- Decide whether support already exists in `vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py`.\n\n### 3) Choose adaptation strategy (new-model capable)\n\n- Reuse existing vLLM architecture if compatible.\n- If architecture is missing or incompatible, implement native support:\n    - add model adapter under `vllm/model_executor/models/`;\n    - add processor under `vllm/transformers_utils/processors/` when needed;\n    - register architecture in `vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py`;\n    - implement explicit weight loading/remap rules (including fp8 scale pairing, KV/QK norm sharding, rope variants).\n- If remote code needs newer transformers symbols, do not upgrade dependency.\n- If unavoidable, copy required modeling files from sibling transformers source and keep scope explicit.\n- If failure is backend-specific (kernel/op/platform), patch minimal required code in `/vllm-workspace/vllm-ascend`.\n\n### 4) Implement minimal code changes (in implementation roots)\n\n- Touch only files required for this model adaptation.\n- Keep weight mapping explicit and auditable.\n- Avoid unrelated refactors.\n\n### 5) Two-stage validation on Ascend (direct run)\n\n#### Stage A: dummy fast gate (recommended first)\n\n- Run from `/workspace` with `--load-format dummy`.\n- Goal: fast validate architecture path / operator path / API path.\n- Do not treat `Application startup complete` as pass by itself; request smoke is mandatory.\n- Require at least:\n    - startup readiness (`/v1/models` 200),\n    - one text request 200,\n    - if VL model, one text+image request 200,\n    - ACLGraph evidence where expected.\n\n#### Stage B: real-weight mandatory gate (must pass before sign-off)\n\n- Remove `--load-format dummy` and validate with real checkpoint.\n- Goal: validate real-only risks:\n    - weight key mapping,\n    - fp8/fp4 dequantization path,\n    - KV/QK norm sharding with real tensor shapes,\n    - load-time/runtime stability.\n- Require HTTP 200 and non-empty output before declaring success.\n- Do not pass Stage B on startup-only evidence.\n\n### 6) Validate inference and features\n\n- Send `GET /v1/models` first.\n- Send at least one OpenAI-compatible text request.\n- For multimodal models, require at least one text+image request.\n- Validate architecture registration and loader path with logs (no unresolved architecture, no fatal missing-key errors).\n- Try feature-first validation: EP + ACLGraph path first; eager path as fallback/isolation.\n- If startup succeeds but first request crashes (false-ready), treat as runtime failure and continue root-cause isolation.\n- For `torch._dynamo` + `interpolate` + `NPU contiguous` failures on VL paths, try `TORCHDYNAMO_DISABLE=1` as diagnostic/stability fallback.\n- For multimodal processor API mismatch (for example `skip_tensor_conversion` signature mismatch), use text-only isolation (`--limit-mm-per-prompt` set image/video/audio to 0) to separate processor issues from core weight loading issues.\n- Capacity baseline by default (single machine): `max-model-len=128k` + `max-num-seqs=16`.\n- Then expand concurrency (e.g., 32/64) if requested or feasible.\n\n### 7) Backport, generate artifacts, and commit in delivery repo\n\n- If implementation happened in `/vllm-workspace/*`, backport minimal final diff to current working repo.\n- Generate test config YAML at `tests/e2e/models/configs/<ModelName>.yaml` following the schema of existing configs (must include `model_name`, `hardware`, `tasks` with accuracy metrics, and `num_fewshot`). Use accuracy results from evaluation to populate metric values.\n- Generate tutorial markdown at `docs/source/tutorials/models/<ModelName>.md` following the standard template (Introduction, Supported Features, Environment Preparation with docker tabs, Deployment with serve script, Functional Verification with curl example, Accuracy Evaluation, Performance). Fill in model-specific details: HF path, hardware requirements, TP size, max-model-len, served-model-name, sample curl, and accuracy table.\n- Update `docs/source/tutorials/models/index.md` to include the new tutorial.\n- Confirm test config YAML and tutorial doc are included in the staged files.\n- Commit code changes once (single signed commit).\n\n### 8) Prepare handoff artifacts\n\n- Write comprehensive Chinese analysis report.\n- Write compact Chinese runbook for server startup and validation commands.\n- Include feature status matrix (supported / unsupported / checkpoint-missing / not-applicable).\n- Include dummy-vs-real validation matrix and explicit non-equivalence notes.\n- Include changed-file list, key logs, and final commit hash.\n- Post the SKILL.md content (or a link to it) as a comment on the originating GitHub issue to document the AI-assisted workflow.\n\n## Quality gate before final answer\n\n- Service starts successfully from `/workspace` with direct command.\n- OpenAI-compatible inference request succeeds (not startup-only).\n- Key feature set is attempted and reported: ACLGraph / EP / flashcomm1 / MTP / multimodal.\n- Capacity baseline (`128k + bs16`) result is reported, or explicit reason why not feasible.\n- **Dummy stage evidence is present (if used), and real-weight stage evidence is present (mandatory).**\n- Test config YAML exists at `tests/e2e/models/configs/<ModelName>.yaml` and follows the established schema (`model_name`, `hardware`, `tasks`, `num_fewshot`).\n- Tutorial doc exists at `docs/source/tutorials/models/<ModelName>.md` and follows the standard template (Introduction, Supported Features, Environment Preparation, Deployment, Functional Verification, Accuracy Evaluation, Performance).\n- Tutorial index at `docs/source/tutorials/models/index.md` includes the new model entry.\n- Exactly one signed commit contains all code changes in current working repo.\n- Final response includes commit hash, file paths, key commands, known limits, and failure reasons where applicable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T02:13:41.814Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents needing seamless integration of Hugging Face or local models with vLLM on Ascend hardware","zh":"适用于需要将Hugging Face或本地模型与vLLM在Ascend硬件上实现无缝集成的AI代理","ja":"Hugging FaceまたはローカルモデルをAscendハードウェアのvLLMとシームレスに統合する必要があるAIエージェントに適しています","ko":"Ascend 하드웨어의 vLLM과 Hugging Face 또는 로컬 모델을 무결점으로 통합해야 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que necesitan una integración perfecta de Hugging Face o modelos locales con vLLM en hardware Ascend","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant une intégration transparente de Hugging Face ou de modèles locaux avec vLLM sur le matériel Ascend","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die eine nahtlose Integration von Hugging Face oder lokalen Modellen mit vLLM auf Ascend-Hardware benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que necessitam integração sem problemas de Hugging Face ou modelos locais com vLLM em hardware Ascend","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих бесшовной интеграции Hugging Face или локальных моделей с vLLM на оборудовании Ascend","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى دمج بدون مشاكل ل Hugging Face أو النماذج المحلية مع vLLM على الأجهزة Ascend"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to adapt models for deterministic validation and single-commit delivery on vLLM-Ascend, leveraging minimal changes and supporting both existing and new architectures with Hugging Face or local models","zh":"赋予代理以适应vLLM-Ascend上的确定性验证和单次提交的模型能力，利用最小的更改并支持现有的和新的Hugging Face或本地模型架构","ja":"vLLM-Ascend上での決定的な検証と1回のコミットでの配信を可能にするモデルを、最小限の変更で適応できるようにエージェントに権限を与え、既存のアーキテクチャと新しいアーキテクチャの両方をHugging Faceまたはローカルモデルでサポートする","ko":"vLLM-Ascend에서 결정적인 검증과 단일 커밋 배포를 위한 모델을 적응시킬 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여, 최소한의 변경으로 기존 및 새로운 아키텍처를 Hugging Face 또는 로컬 모델로 지원합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a adaptar modelos para una validación determinista y una entrega de un solo compromiso en vLLM-Ascend, aprovechando cambios mínimos y admitiendo tanto arquitecturas existentes como nuevas con Hugging Face o modelos locales","fr":"Permet aux agents d''adapter les modèles pour une validation déterministe et une livraison en un seul engagement sur vLLM-Ascend, en exploitant des changements minimaux et en prenant en charge à la fois les architectures existantes et nouvelles avec Hugging Face ou des modèles locaux","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Modelle für eine deterministische Validierung und eine Single-Commit-Lieferung auf vLLM-Ascend anzupassen, wobei minimaler Aufwand erforderlich ist und sowohl bestehende als auch neue Architekturen mit Hugging Face oder lokalen Modellen unterstützt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a adaptarem modelos para validação determinística e entrega de um único commit no vLLM-Ascend, aproveitando alterações mínimas e suportando tanto arquiteturas existentes quanto novas com Hugging Face ou modelos locais","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью адаптировать модели для детерминированной валидации и доставки в один коммит на vLLM-Ascend, используя минимальные изменения и поддерживая как существующие, так и новые архитектуры с Hugging Face или локальными моделями","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تعديل النماذج للتحقق من الصحة التحديدية وتسليم التعديل الفردي على vLLM-Ascend، مستفيدا من التغييرات القصوى ودعم الهياكل المعمارية الموجودة والجديدة مع Hugging Face أو النماذج المحلية"},"useCases":{"en":["Adapting Hugging Face models for vLLM-Ascend compatibility","Deploying new model architectures on vLLM-Ascend with minimal modifications","Validating model performance on Ascend hardware with deterministic results"],"zh":["将Hugging Face模型适配为vLLM-Ascend兼容性","在vLLM-Ascend上部署具有最小修改的新模型架构","在Ascend硬件上验证模型性能以获得确定性的结果"],"ja":["Hugging FaceモデルをvLLM-Ascendと互換性のあるように適応させる","vLLM-Ascend上に最小限の変更で新しいモデルアーキテクチャをデプロイする","Ascendハードウェア上で決定的な結果をもってモデルパフォーマンスを検証する"],"ko":["Hugging Face 모델을 vLLM-Ascend와 호환되는 형태로 적응시키기","vLLM-Ascend에서 최소한의 수정으로 새로운 모델 아키텍처를 배포하기","Ascend 하드웨어에서 결정적인 결과를 얻어 모델 성능을 검증하기"],"es":["Adaptar modelos de Hugging Face para la compatibilidad con vLLM-Ascend","Implementar nuevas arquitecturas de modelos en vLLM-Ascend con modificaciones mínimas","Validar el rendimiento del modelo en hardware Ascend con resultados deterministas"],"fr":["Adapter les modèles de Hugging Face pour la compatibilité avec vLLM-Ascend","Déployer de nouvelles architectures de modèles sur vLLM-Ascend avec des modifications minimales","Valider les performances du modèle sur le matériel Ascend avec des résultats déterministes"],"de":["Hugging Face-Modelle für die Kompatibilität mit vLLM-Ascend anpassen","Neue Modellarchitekturen auf vLLM-Ascend mit minimalen Modifikationen bereitstellen","Modellleistung auf Ascend-Hardware m