enz in Entwicklungsprojekten","Kompatibilität mit Node.js-Anwendungen","Einfach zu bedienen und zu konfigurieren"],"pt":["Substituição direta para o node:sqlite","Solução eficiente para desenvolvedores Node.js","Fácil integração com projetos existentes","Suporte a recursos avançados do SQLite","Melhoria do desempenho e escalabilidade"],"ru":["Прямая замена node:sqlite","Эффективное решение для разработчиков Node.js","Легкая интеграция с существующими проектами","Поддержка расширенных функций SQLite","Улучшение производительности и масштабируемости"],"ar":["بديل مباشر لـ node:sqlite","حل فعال للمطورين Node.js","تكامل سهل مع المشاريع الحالية","دعم الميزات المتقدمة لـ SQLite","تحسين الأداء والتحجيم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Node.js SQLite替代","tpp是什么","如何使用tpp","tpp安装指南","tpp与SQLite比较","Node.js数据存储解决方案","tpp文档","tpp示例"],"ja":["Node.jsのSQLite代替","tppとは","tppの使い方","tppのインストールガイド","tppとSQLiteの比較","Node.jsのデータストレージソリューション","tppドキュメント","tppの例"],"ko":["Node.js SQLite 대체","tpp란 무엇인가","tpp 사용 방법","tpp 설치 가이드","tpp와 SQLite 비교","Node.js 데이터 저장소 솔루션","tpp 문서","tpp 예시"],"es":["tpp","node:sqlite","herramientas de inteligencia artificial","desarrollo de aplicaciones","bases de datos","cómo usar tpp","tpp vs node:sqlite","instalación de tpp","guía de configuración de tpp"],"fr":["tpp","node:sqlite","outils d''intelligence artificielle","développement d''applications","bases de données","comment utiliser tpp","tpp vs node:sqlite","installation de tpp","guide de configuration de tpp"],"de":["tpp","node:sqlite","KI-Tools","Anwendungsentwicklung","Datenbanken","wie man tpp verwendet","tpp vs node:sqlite","Installation von tpp","Konfigurationsanleitung für tpp"],"pt":["tpp","node:sqlite","substituto do node:sqlite","ferramenta de desenvolvimento","ИИ Агенты","como usar tpp","tpp vs node:sqlite","instalar tpp","guia de configuração do tpp"],"ru":["tpp","node:sqlite","замена node:sqlite","инструмент разработки","ИИ Агенты","как использовать tpp","tpp vs node:sqlite","установить tpp","руководство по настройке tpp"],"ar":["tpp","node:sqlite","بديل node:sqlite","أداة تطوير","AI Agents","كيفية استخدام tpp","tpp vs node:sqlite","تثبيت tpp","دليل إعداد tpp"]}},"owner":"photostructure","repo":"node-sqlite","repoPath":"photostructure/node-sqlite","stars":6,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T03:34:31Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tpp","description":"Work on a Technical Project Plan - research, design, implement, or complete tasks based on current phase. Use when starting or continuing work on a TPP.","bodyPreview":"# Work on TPP\n\nMake progress on the referenced Technical Project Plan. Determine the current phase and take appropriate action.\n\n## Required Reading First\n\nBefore any work, you MUST read:\n\n- [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) - Project rules and patterns\n- [SIMPLE-DESIGN.md](doc/reference/SIMPLE-DESIGN.md) - Kent Beck''s Simple Design\n- [TDD.md](doc/reference/TDD.md) - Test-driven development\n- [TPP-GUIDE.md](doc/reference/TPP-GUIDE.md) - TPP style guide\n\n## Process\n\n### 1. Read the TPP\n\nFind and read the re","body":"# Work on TPP\n\nMake progress on the referenced Technical Project Plan. Determine the current phase and take appropriate action.\n\n## Required Reading First\n\nBefore any work, you MUST read:\n\n- [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) - Project rules and patterns\n- [SIMPLE-DESIGN.md](doc/reference/SIMPLE-DESIGN.md) - Kent Beck''s Simple Design\n- [TDD.md](doc/reference/TDD.md) - Test-driven development\n- [TPP-GUIDE.md](doc/reference/TPP-GUIDE.md) - TPP style guide\n\n## Process\n\n### 1. Read the TPP\n\nFind and read the referenced TPP from `doc/todo/` (named `${priority}-${desc}.md`). Identify the current phase from the checklist.\n\n### 2. Take Action Based on Phase\n\n| Phase                    | Action                                                                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Research & Planning**  | Read referenced docs and code. Gather context. Update TPP with findings. |\n| **Write breaking tests** | Follow TDD approach - write failing tests first.                         |\n| **Design alternatives**  | Iterate on design with critiques, consider multiple approaches.          |\n| **Breakdown of tasks**   | Create specific, verifiable task list with commands.                     |\n| **Implementation**       | Work through tasks sequentially. Update TPP as you go.                   |\n| **Review & Refinement**  | Review changed code. Address issues. Check API compatibility.            |\n| **Final Integration**    | Run full test suite. Verify all acceptance criteria.                     |\n| **Review**               | Present completion proof to user.                                        |\n\n### 3. Update the TPP\n\nAfter each work session:\n\n- Check off completed phases/tasks\n- Add discoveries to Tribal Knowledge\n- Document failed approaches and why\n- Keep under 400 lines (trim redundancy)\n\n### 4. Completion\n\nWhen all phases are complete:\n\n1. Run verification commands from the TPP\n2. Ensure all tests pass (`npm test`)\n3. Review all changes for API compatibility with `node:sqlite`\n4. Present proof of completion to user\n5. After user approval, move TPP to `doc/done/` with date prefix\n\n```bash\n# Example: P01-fix-aggregate-null.md -> 20250203-P01-fix-aggregate-null.md\ngit mv doc/todo/P01-feature.md doc/done/$(date +%Y%m%d)-P01-feature.md\n```\n\n## Phase Details\n\n### Research & Planning\n\n- Read all \"Required reading\" in the TPP\n- Explore referenced source files\n- Check Node.js SQLite and better-sqlite3 for API reference\n- Web search for prior art if needed\n- Consult `../node-addon-api/` for N-API questions\n- Document findings in the TPP\n\n### Design Alternatives\n\n- Generate 2-4 approaches\n- Critique each for simplicity, testability, maintainability\n- Consider API compatibility with `node:sqlite`\n- Iterate at least 3 times\n- Document final recommendation in TPP\n\n### Task Breakdown\n\nEach task must include:\n\n- Clear deliverable\n- Files to change\n- Success criteria\n- Verification command\n\n### Implementation\n\n- Work tasks sequentially\n- Mark tasks complete as you go\n- Run verification after each task\n- Update TPP with any discoveries\n- Follow N-API best practices (see `../node-addon-api/`)\n\n## Remember\n\n- Transfer expertise, not just instructions\n- Document what didn''t work and why\n- Ask for clarification when uncertain\n- The next engineer should be able to continue seamlessly\n- Maintain API compatibility with `node:sqlite`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T01:36:07.658Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing structured project planning and execution using Technical Project Plans (TPP) and Test-Driven Development (TDD)","zh":"非常适合需要使用技术项目计划（TPP）和测试驱动开发（TDD）进行结构化项目规划和执行的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントがテクニカルプロジェクトプラン（TPP）とテスト駆動開発（TDD）を使用して構造化されたプロジェクト計画と実行が必要な場合に最適","ko":"구조화된 프로젝트 계획 및 실행을 위해 기술 프로젝트 계획(TPP) 및 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)을 사용하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una planificación y ejecución de proyectos estructuradas utilizando Planes de Proyecto Técnico (TPP) y Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD)","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une planification et une exécution de projet structurées en utilisant des Plans de Projet Technique (TPP) et le Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD)","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine strukturierte Projektplanung und -ausführung unter Verwendung von Technischen Projektplänen (TPP) und testgetriebenem Entwickeln (TDD) benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de planejamento e execução de projetos estruturados usando Planos de Projeto Técnicos (TPP) e Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходим структурированный планирование и выполнение проектов с использованием Технических планов проектов (TPP) и Разработки, управляемой тестами (TDD)","ar":"مثالي لمراقبي التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تخطيط وتنفيذ مشاريع منظمين باستخدام خطط المشروع الفنية (TPP) وتطوير مدفوع بالاختبار (TDD)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Kent Beck''s Simple Design principles, adhere to TPP style guides, and leverage SQLite databases for efficient project management, utilizing TDD for robust testing and validation","zh":"赋予代理实现Kent Beck的简单设计原则，遵循TPP风格指南，并利用SQLite数据库进行高效的项目管理，使用TDD进行强大的测试和验证","ja":"エージェントがKent Beckのシンプルデザインの原則を実施し、TPPスタイルガイドに従い、SQLiteデータベースを使用して効率的なプロジェクト管理を行い、TDDを使用して強力なテストと検証を行う","ko":"에이전트가 켄트 벡의 단순 설계 원칙을 구현하고 TPP 스타일 가이드를 따르며 SQLite 데이터베이스를 사용하여 효율적인 프로젝트 관리를 수행하고 TDD를 사용하여 강력한 테스트 및 검증을 수행할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar los principios de Diseño Simple de Kent Beck, adherirse a las guías de estilo de TPP y aprovechar las bases de datos SQLite para una gestión de proyectos eficiente, utilizando TDD para pruebas y validación robustas","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre les principes de Conception Simple de Kent Beck, d''adhérer aux guides de style de TPP et d''utiliser les bases de données SQLite pour une gestion de projet efficace, en utilisant TDD pour des tests et une validation robustes","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Prinzipien des einfachen Designs von Kent Beck umzusetzen, sich an die Stilrichtlinien von TPP zu halten und SQLite-Datenbanken für eine effiziente Projektverwaltung zu nutzen, unter Verwendung von TDD für robuste Tests und Validierung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar os princípios de Design Simples de Kent Beck, aderir às diretrizes de estilo do TPP e aproveitar os bancos de dados SQLite para gerenciamento de projetos eficiente, utilizando o TDD para testes e validação robustos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать принципы простого дизайна Кента Бека, придерживаться руководств по стилю TPP и использовать базы данных SQLite для эффективного управления проектами, используя TDD для надежного тестирования и проверки","ar":"تمكين المراقبين من تنفيذ مبادئ التصميم البسيط لKent Beck ، والالتزام bởi دلالات أسلوب TPP ، وتحقيق قواعد بيانات SQLite لأدارة المشاريع الفعالة ، باستخدام TDD للاختبار والتحقق القوي"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing TPP-guided project development","Conducting test-driven development with TDD","Managing project phases using SQLite databases"],"zh":["实施TPP指导的项目开发","使用TDD进行测试驱动开发","使用SQLite数据库管理项目阶段"],"ja":["TPPガイドによるプロジェクト開発の実施","TDDを使用したテスト駆動開発","SQLiteデータベースを使用したプロジェクトフェーズの管理"],"ko":["TPP 가이드에 따른 프로젝트 개발 구현","TDD를 사용한 테스트 주도 개발","SQLite 데이터베이스를 사용한 프로젝트 단계 관리"],"es":["Implementación del desarrollo de proyectos guiado por TPP","Realización del desarrollo dirigido por pruebas con TDD","Gestión de fases de proyecto utilizando bases de datos SQLite"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre du développement de projet guidé par TPP","Réalisations du développement piloté par les tests avec TDD","Gestion des phases de projet en utilisant des bases de données SQLite"],"de":["Implementierung der Projektentwicklung unter Anleitung von TPP","Durchführung der testgetriebenen Entwicklung mit TDD","Verwaltung von Projektphasen unter Verwendung von SQLite-Datenbanken"],"pt":["Implementação do desenvolvimento de projetos orientado por TPP","Realização do desenvolvimento dirigido por testes com TDD","Gerenciamento de fases de projeto usando bancos de dados SQLite"],"ru":["Реализация разработки проектов, управляемой TPP","Проведение разработки, управляемой тестами, с использованием TDD","Управление фазами проекта с использованием баз данных SQLite"],"ar":["تنفيذ تطوير المشاريع الموجه بواسطة TPP","إجراء تطوير مدفوع بالاختبار باستخدام TDD","إدارة مراحل المشروع باستخدام قواعد بيانات SQLite"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires prior reading of CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md, and TPP-GUIDE.md","SQLite database replacement needed"],"zh":["需要先阅读CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md, 和TPP-GUIDE.md","需要替换SQLite数据库"],"ja":["CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md, およびTPP-GUIDE.mdを事前に読む必要がある","SQLiteデータベースの置き換えが必要"],"ko":["CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md, 및 TPP-GUIDE.md를 먼저 읽어야 함","SQLite 데이터베이스를 대체해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la lectura previa de CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md y TPP-GUIDE.md","Se necesita reemplazar la base de datos SQLite"],"fr":["Nécessite la lecture préalable de CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md et TPP-GUIDE.md","Remplacement de la base de données SQLite nécessaire"],"de":["Erfordert das vorherige Lesen von CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md und TPP-GUIDE.md","Ersetzen der SQLite-Datenbank erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer leitura prévia de CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md e TPP-GUIDE.md","Substituição do banco de dados SQLite necessária"],"ru":["Требует предварительного чтения CLAUDE.md, SIMPLE-DESIGN.md, TDD.md и TPP-GUIDE.md","Необходимо заменить базу данных SQLite"],"ar":["يتطلب قراءة سابقة من CLAUDE.md ، SIMPLE-DESIGN.md ، TDD.md و TPP-GUIDE.md","تحديث قاعدة بيانات SQLite ضروري"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"e7b4578bbdcad8cbaa6b9c2bcd9df9b47b853f141cc0d66b51af1a8de353db0b","qualityScore":37}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('omniaura/omniclaw/migrate-to-channels', 'community', 'omniaura', 'omniclaw', 'omniaura/omniclaw', 'migrate-to-channels', 4, 1, 37, '2026-02-28T18:12:17Z', '2026-03-01T05:20:57.777Z', 'c4ec350aa88665b722bd65195cb40ba14a29cb2fe8fc6bbd9b82d49d752d31ba', '{"id":"omniaura/omniclaw/migrate-to-channels","name":"migrate-to-channels","description":{"zh":"migrate-to-channels 是一个始终在线的编码代理，驻扎在您的团队聊天中，提供实时编码协助","ja":"migrate-to-channels は、常にオンラインのコーディングエージェントで、グループチャットに駐在し、リアルタイムのコーディング支援を提供します","ko":"migrate-to-channels 는 그룹 채팅中的 실시간 코딩 지원을 제공하는 항상 온라인 코딩 에이전트입니다","es":"migrate-to-channels es un agente de código siempre activo que vive en tus chats de grupo, mejorando tu productividad","fr":"migrate-to-channels est un agent de codage toujours actif qui vit dans vos chats de groupe, améliorant votre productivité","de":"migrate-to-channels ist ein immer aktiver Code-Agent, der in Ihren Gruppenchats lebt und Ihre Produktivität verbessert","pt":"O agente de codificação AI ''migrate-to-channels'' é um assistente de codificação sempre ativo que vive nos chats de grupo, ajudando a migrar para canais de forma eficiente","ru":"ИИ агент ''migrate-to-channels'' является всегда-активным помощником по кодированию, живущим в групповых чатах, помогающим мигрировать на каналы эффективно","ar":"وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي ''migrate-to-channels'' هو مساعد ترميز دائم الفعالية يعيش في المحادثات الجماعية، مما يساعد في الهجرة إلى القنوات بفعالية","en":"Always-on coding agent that lives in your group chats"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 migrate-to-channels","ja":"AIエージェント migrate-to-channels","ko":"AI 에이전트 migrate-to-channels","es":"Agente de código siempre activo: migrate-to-channels","fr":"Agent de codage toujours actif: migrate-to-channels","de":"Immer aktiver Code-Agent: migrate-to-channels","pt":"Migrar para Canais com Agente de Codificação AI","ru":"Миграция на Каналы с Помощью ИИ Агента","ar":"هجرة إلى القنوات مع وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي","en":"migrate-to-channels"},"description":{"zh":"migrate-to-channels 是一个始终在线的编码代理，驻扎在您的团队聊天中，提供实时编码协助","ja":"migrate-to-channels は、常にオンラインのコーディングエージェントで、グループチャットに駐在し、リアルタイムのコーディング支援を提供します","ko":"migrate-to-channels 는 그룹 채팅中的 실시간 코딩 지원을 제공하는 항상 온라인 코딩 에이전트입니다","es":"migrate-to-channels es un agente de código siempre activo que vive en tus chats de grupo, mejorando tu productividad","fr":"migrate-to-channels est un agent de codage toujours actif qui vit dans vos chats de groupe, améliorant votre productivité","de":"migrate-to-channels ist ein immer aktiver Code-Agent, der in Ihren Gruppenchats lebt und Ihre Produktivität verbessert","pt":"O agente de codificação AI ''migrate-to-channels'' é um assistente de codificação sempre ativo que vive nos chats de grupo, ajudando a migrar para canais de fo...","ru":"ИИ агент ''migrate-to-channels'' является всегда-активным помощником по кодированию, живущим в групповых чатах, помогающим мигрировать на каналы эффективно","ar":"وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي ''migrate-to-channels'' هو مساعد ترميز دائم الفعالية يعيش في المحادثات الجماعية، مما يساعد في الهجرة إلى القنوات بفعالية","en":"Always-on coding agent that lives in your group chats"},"definition":{"en":"Always-on coding agent that lives in your group chats"},"features":{"zh":["实时编码协助","团队聊天集成","支持多种编程语言","提供代码自动补全","支持代码调试"],"ja":["リアルタイムコーディング支援","グループチャット統合","複数のプログラミング言語をサポート","コード自動補完を提供","コードデバッグをサポート"],"ko":["실시간 코딩 지원","그룹 채팅 통합","여러 프로그래밍 언어 지원","코드 자동 완성을 제공","코드 디버깅 지원"],"es":["Codificación siempre activa","Integración con chats de grupo","Mejora de la productividad","Automatización de tareas","Soporte para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Codage toujours actif","Intégration avec les chats de groupe","Amélioration de la productivité","Automatisation des tâches","Support pour les développeurs"],"de":["Immer aktive Codierung","Integration mit Gruppenchats","Produktivitätssteigerung","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Unterstützung für Entwickler"],"pt":["Assistente de codificação sempre ativo","Integração com chats de grupo","Migração para canais eficiente","Melhoria da produtividade do time de desenvolvimento","Suporte a linguagens de programação como React e Python"],"ru":["Всегда-активный помощник по кодированию","Интеграция с групповыми чатами","Эффективная миграция на каналы","Повышение производительности команды разработчиков","Поддержка языков программирования như React и Python"],"ar":["مساعد ترميز دائم الفعالية","التكامل مع المحادثات الجماعية","الهجرة إلى القنوات بفعالية","تحسين إنتاجية فريق التطوير","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل React و Python"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 migrate-to-channels","什么是 AI 智能代理","migrate-to-channels 替代品","migrate-to-channels 安装","migrate-to-channels 教程","实时编码协助工具"],"ja":["migrate-to-channels の使用方法","AI エージェントとは","migrate-to-channels の代替","migrate-to-channels のインストール","migrate-to-channels のチュートリアル","リアルタイムコーディング支援ツール"],"ko":["migrate-to-channels 사용법","AI 에이전트란","migrate-to-channels 대안","migrate-to-channels 설치","migrate-to-channels 튜토리얼","실시간 코딩 지원 도구"],"es":["cómo usar migrate-to-channels","agente de inteligencia artificial","herramientas de codificación","migrate-to-channels alternativa","migrate-to-channels vs otros","instalación de migrate-to-channels","guía de configuración de migrate-to-channels"],"fr":["comment utiliser migrate-to-channels","outil d''intelligence artificielle","outils de codage","migrate-to-channels alternative","migrate-to-channels vs autres","installation de migrate-to-channels","guide de configuration de migrate-to-channels"],"de":["wie man migrate-to-channels verwendet","künstlicher Intelligenz-Agent","Codierungstools","migrate-to-channels Alternative","migrate-to-channels vs andere","Installation von migrate-to-channels","Konfigurationsanleitung für migrate-to-channels"],"pt":["como usar agente de codificação AI","o que é agente de codificação AI","migrar para canais","agente de codificação AI vs outros","instalar agente de codificação AI","guia de configuração do agente de codificação AI","desenvolvimento de software com agente de codificação AI"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ агент","что такое ИИ агент","миграция на каналы","ИИ агент vs другие","установить ИИ агент","руководство по настройке ИИ агента","разработка программного обеспечения с ИИ агентом"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي","ما هو وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي","هجرة إلى القنوات","وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي مقابل غيره","تثبيت وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي","دليل إعداد وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي","تطوير البرمجيات مع وكيل الترميز الإصطناعي"]}},"owner":"omniaura","repo":"omniclaw","repoPath":"omniaura/omniclaw","stars":4,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T18:12:17Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"migrate-to-channels","description":"Migrate existing multi-agent Discord/Slack setup to the new agent/server/category/channel context architecture. Restructures group workspaces into isolated per-channel notebooks with shared category and agent identity layers.","bodyPreview":"# Migrate to Channel Architecture\n\nThis skill migrates your existing OmniClaw setup from the flat `groups/` workspace model to the new layered context architecture:\n\n```\ngroups/\n  agents/{agentId}/CLAUDE.md     ← agent identity (shared across channels)\n  servers/{server}/{category}/    ← category team workspace\n  servers/{server}/{category}/{channel}/  ← isolated channel notebook\n  channels/{name}/               ← non-server channels (WhatsApp, Telegram)\n```\n\n## What This Skill Does\n\n1. **Inspec","body":"# Migrate to Channel Architecture\n\nThis skill migrates your existing OmniClaw setup from the flat `groups/` workspace model to the new layered context architecture:\n\n```\ngroups/\n  agents/{agentId}/CLAUDE.md     ← agent identity (shared across channels)\n  servers/{server}/{category}/    ← category team workspace\n  servers/{server}/{category}/{channel}/  ← isolated channel notebook\n  channels/{name}/               ← non-server channels (WhatsApp, Telegram)\n```\n\n## What This Skill Does\n\n1. **Inspects** the live database — reads all `channel_subscriptions`, `agents`, and their current workspace mappings\n2. **Consolidates** legacy agent entries that share the same persona\n3. **Proposes** a folder mapping for each channel (server → category → channel path)\n4. **Creates** new directories and CLAUDE.md stubs for missing layers\n5. **Updates** `channel_folder`, `category_folder`, `agent_context_folder` in the DB for each subscription/agent\n6. **Sets `is_primary`** correctly on each channel''s subscriptions\n7. **Verifies** agents without new fields still work (backward compat)\n\n---\n\n## Known Gotchas (from real migration)\n\n### 1. Consolidate legacy agent entries first\n\nIn older OmniClaw setups, each channel got its own agent entry (e.g., `landing-astro-discord`, `spec-discord`, `backend-discord`) even though they all share the same persona. These are **not separate agents** — they''re just channels.\n\n**Before migrating**, merge them: re-point their subscriptions to the canonical agent and delete the stubs.\n\n```sql\n-- Example: landing-astro-discord was just another PeytonOmni channel\n-- Move its subs to ditto-discord (if not already there)\nINSERT OR IGNORE INTO channel_subscriptions (channel_jid, agent_id, trigger_pattern, requires_trigger, priority, is_primary, discord_bot_id, discord_guild_id, created_at)\nSELECT channel_jid, ''ditto-discord'', trigger_pattern, requires_trigger, priority, is_primary, discord_bot_id, discord_guild_id, created_at\nFROM channel_subscriptions WHERE agent_id = ''landing-astro-discord'';\n\nDELETE FROM channel_subscriptions WHERE agent_id = ''landing-astro-discord'';\nDELETE FROM agents WHERE id = ''landing-astro-discord'';\nDELETE FROM registered_groups WHERE folder = ''landing-astro-discord'';\n```\n\n### 2. Set `agent_context_folder` — or identity breaks\n\nWithout `agent_context_folder`, the fallback identity injection fires using `agent.name` from the DB (e.g., \"Landing Astro\", \"Ditto Discord\") — **not** the persona name. The agent will say \"I am Landing Astro\" instead of \"I am PeytonOmni\".\n\nSet this immediately after adding the agent identity file:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE agents SET agent_context_folder = ''agents/peytonomi''\nWHERE id IN (''ditto-discord'', ''landing-astro-discord'');\n```\n\n### 3. The identity fallback injects the bot key, not the numeric Discord ID\n\nWhen `agent_context_folder` is NULL, the injected identity block contains the bot key string (e.g., `OCPEYTON`, `PRIMARY`) not the numeric Discord bot ID. This causes the agent to report conflicting identity info. The fix is always to set `agent_context_folder`.\n\n### 4. `is_primary` controls more than routing — it controls channel name resolution\n\n`is_primary` determines:\n- Which Discord bot handles the channel (sends messages, reactions)\n- Which agent''s name is used as the display name when building channel lists\n- Which subscriptions fire as a fallback when no trigger is explicitly matched\n\nIn a multi-agent channel (e.g., PeytonOmni + OCPeyton both in `#spec`), set `is_primary = 1` **only on the human-persona agent** (e.g., `ditto-discord`). The tool agent (`ocpeyton-discord`) should have `is_primary = 0` so it only responds to explicit `@OCPeyton` mentions and never fires via fallback.\n\nIf `is_primary` is wrong, you''ll see another agent''s name appear as a channel name in the multi-channel list (e.g., \"OCPeyton\" showing up as a channel name in PeytonOmni''s channel list).\n\n```sql\n-- Set primary correctly for each channel\nUPDATE channel_subscriptions SET is_primary = 1\nWHERE agent_id = ''ditto-discord'';  -- persona agent owns the channel\n\nUPDATE channel_subscriptions SET is_primary = 0\nWHERE agent_id = ''ocpeyton-discord'';  -- tool agent never owns\n```\n\n---\n\n## Steps\n\n### Step 1: Inspect current state\n\n```bash\nsqlite3 store/messages.db \"\nSELECT id, name, agent_context_folder FROM agents ORDER BY id;\nSELECT ''---'';\nSELECT channel_jid, agent_id, trigger_pattern, is_primary, channel_folder FROM channel_subscriptions ORDER BY channel_jid, agent_id;\n\"\n```\n\nLook for:\n- Multiple agent entries that are really the same persona (different channel, same trigger/bot)\n- Agents with `agent_context_folder` = NULL (identity will be wrong)\n- Channels where `is_primary` isn''t set correctly\n\n### Step 2: Consolidate legacy agent entries\n\nIdentify agents that are actually just channels for an existing persona. Re-point their subscriptions and delete the agent entry (see gotcha #1 above).\n\n### Step 3: Create agent identity files\n\nFor each distinct persona, create `groups/agents/{id}/CLAUDE.md`:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p groups/agents/peytonomi\ncat > groups/agents/peytonomi/CLAUDE.md << ''EOF''\n# PeytonOmni Identity\nYou are **PeytonOmni** (@PeytonOmni), ...\nEOF\n```\n\nThen set `agent_context_folder` in the DB immediately (gotcha #2).\n\n### Step 4: Create category directories and CLAUDE.md stubs\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p groups/servers/{server}/{category}/{channel}\n```\n\nCreate a `CLAUDE.md` in each category folder documenting the project context shared across channels.\n\n### Step 5: Migrate legacy folder content to new channel dirs\n\nFor each old flat group folder (e.g., `spec-discord/`, `agentflow-discord/`), copy its contents into the new channel workspace. Use `cp` — never `mv` at this stage, so the original is preserved as a fallback.\n\n```bash\n# Copy all files except logs/ from old folder to new channel dir\nfind groups/spec-discord -maxdepth 1 -not -name ''logs'' -not -path ''groups/spec-discord'' \\\n  -exec cp -r {} groups/servers/omni-aura/ditto-assistant/spec/ \\;\n```\n\nRepeat for each old folder → new path mapping. After copying, verify the new dirs have the expected files.\n\n**If a channel has content in two legacy locations** (e.g., both `ocpeyton-discord/` and `landing-astro-discord/` map to the same new channel), merge them manually — copy one first, then copy the other, skipping any collisions.\n\n#### Offer to clean up old folders\n\nAfter all content is verified in the new locations, use `AskUserQuestion` to ask the user:\n\n> All legacy folder content has been copied to the new channel structure. Want to delete the old folders?\n>\n> - **Yes, delete them** — removes the duplicates, keeps `groups/` clean\n> - **No, keep them** — I''ll show you where everything lives so you can clean up manually later\n\n**If yes:** first check whether any containers are actively running — deleting a folder while a container has it virtiofs-mounted can break the mount mid-run (the host rename makes the path disappear inside the container).\n\n```bash\n# Check for running omniclaw containers\ncontainer list 2>/dev/null | grep omniclaw || echo \"No containers running\"\n```\n\nIf containers are running, use `AskUserQuestion` to ask:\n\n> Some agent containers are currently running. Deleting their workspace folders now could break an in-progress response. What would you like to do?\n>\n> - **Wait and check again** — I''ll re-check in a moment\n> - **Stop the service now** — safest option, agents will pick up again on next restart\n\n**If wait:** re-run the container list check and loop until clear, then delete without stopping the service:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf groups/spec-discord groups/agentflow-discord groups/ditto-discord # etc.\n```\n\n**If stop the service:** unload, delete, reload:\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.omniclaw.plist\nrm -rf groups/spec-discord groups/agentflow-discord groups/ditto-discord # etc.\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.omniclaw.plist\n```\n\n**If no containers running:** delete directly:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf groups/spec-discord groups/agentflow-discord groups/ditto-discord # etc.\n```\n\n**If no:** print a summary table of old → new paths so the user knows where to look:\n\n```\nLegacy folder                          → New location\ngroups/spec-discord/                   → groups/servers/omni-aura/ditto-assistant/spec/\ngroups/agentflow-discord/              → groups/servers/omni-aura/omniaura/agentflow/\ngroups/ditto-discord/                  → groups/servers/omni-aura/omniaura/agent-debug/\n...\n```\n\n#### Handle orphaned folders\n\nSome old folders may have no active DB entry (no `registered_groups` row, no `channel_subscriptions`). These are stale experiments. Show the user a list and ask if they want them deleted too. Safe to delete if they''re just a CLAUDE.md — worth reviewing first if they have real content.\n\n```bash\n# Find folders with no DB entry\nfor f in groups/*/; do\n  name=$(basename \"$f\")\n  count=$(sqlite3 store/messages.db \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM registered_groups WHERE folder=''$name''\")\n  [ \"$count\" = \"0\" ] && echo \"Orphaned: $f ($(ls $f | grep -v logs | wc -l | tr -d '' '') files)\"\ndone\n```\n\n### Step 6: Update subscriptions with channel/category folders\n\n```sql\nUPDATE channel_subscriptions\nSET channel_folder = ''servers/omni-aura/ditto-assistant/spec'',\n    category_folder = ''servers/omni-aura/ditto-assistant''\nWHERE channel_jid = ''dc:...'' AND agent_id = ''ditto-discord'';\n```\n\n### Step 7: Set `is_primary` correctly\n\n```sql\n-- Persona agent owns all channels\nUPDATE channel_subscriptions SET is_primary = 1 WHERE agent_id = ''ditto-discord'';\n-- Tool agents never own\nUPDATE channel_subscriptions SET is_primary = 0 WHERE agent_id = ''ocpeyton-discord'';\n```\n\n### Step 8: Strip extra mounts from Discord agents\n\nDiscord agents should not have host filesystem mounts. They should clone repos into their own workspace rather than reading from the host. Legacy `additionalMounts` in `registered_groups.container_config` give Discord agents access to the host filesystem, which can cause confusion (agents following stale docs to wrong paths) and is unnecessary security surface.\n\n**Remove `container_config` from all Discord registered_groups:**\n\n```sql\n-- NULL out container_config for all Discord channels (dc: prefix)\nUPDATE registered_groups\nSET container_config = NULL\nWHERE jid LIKE ''dc:%'';\n```\n\nIf any channel genuinely needs custom mounts (e.g., a local dev agent), restore only that channel''s config explicitly:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE registered_groups\nSET container_config = ''{\"additionalMounts\":[...]}''\nWHERE folder = ''local-dev-agent'';\n```\n\n**Set `nonMainReadOnly: true` in the mount allowlist:**\n\nEdit `~/.config/omniclaw/mount-allowlist.json` and set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nonMainReadOnly\": true\n}\n```\n\nThis is belt-and-suspenders: even if `container_config` is accidentally set again, the allowlist prevents any non-main agent from getting write access to extra mounts. Discord agents that need to read/write code should clone the repo into `/workspace/group/` or `/workspace/extra/` and work from there.\n\n### Step 9: Restart and verify\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.omniclaw.plist\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.omniclaw.plist\n```\n\nAsk each agent: \"what are your debug info / loaded contexts?\" — verify:\n- Identity name matches the persona (not the DB agent name)\n- `/workspace/agent/CLAUDE.md` appears in loaded contexts\n- Channel list shows real channel names, not agent names\n\n---\n\n### Step 10: Remove any legacy heartbeat config\n\nThe heartbeat feature has been removed. Use scheduled tasks (`create_task`) instead — they''re more flexible and don''t silently re-create themselves on restart.\n\nIf any agents or groups had heartbeat configured, it will be automatically NULLed out on first startup (the migration runs in `createSchema()`). But you can also clean it up manually:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE registered_groups SET heartbeat = NULL WHERE heartbeat IS NOT NULL;\nUPDATE agents SET heartbeat = NULL WHERE heartbeat IS NOT NULL;\nDELETE FROM scheduled_tasks WHERE id LIKE ''heartbeat-%'';\n```\n\nAny `## Heartbeat` sections in existing `CLAUDE.md` files are now inert (the system no longer reads them). You can leave them as documentation or migrate the content to a regular scheduled task.\n\n---\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\n- Agents without `agent_context_folder` → no `/workspace/agent/` mount, identity via `agentName` fallback (works but name may be wrong — see gotcha #2)\n- Subscriptions without `channel_folder` → workspace falls back to agent folder (unchanged behavior)\n- Subscriptions without `category_folder` → no `/workspace/category/` mount (unchanged behavior)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:20:57.777Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for OmniClaw Agents needing to transition from a flat workspace model to a layered context architecture","zh":"适用于需要从平面工作空间模型转换为分层上下文架构的OmniClaw代理","ja":"OmniClawエージェントがフラットなワークスペースモデルから階層化されたコンテキストアーキテクチャに移行する必要がある場合に最適","ko":"평면 작업 공간 모델에서 계층화된 컨텍스트 아키텍처로 전환해야 하는 OmniClaw 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes OmniClaw que necesitan transitar de un modelo de espacio de trabajo plano a una arquitectura de contexto en capas","fr":"Parfait pour les agents OmniClaw ayant besoin de passer d''un modèle de espace de travail plat à une architecture de contexte en couches","de":"Perfekt für OmniClaw-Agents, die von einem flachen Arbeitsbereichsmodell zu einer schichtbasierten Kontextarchitektur wechseln müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes OmniClaw que precisam fazer a transição de um modelo de espaço de trabalho plano para uma arquitetura de contexto em camadas","ru":"Идеально для агентов OmniClaw, которым необходимо перейти от плоской модели рабочего пространства к архитектуре контекста в слоях","ar":"مثالي لعمال OmniClaw الذين يحتاجون إلى الانتقال من نموذج مساحة عمل مسطحة إلى هندسة سياق متعددة الطبقات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to restructure their existing setup into a hierarchical organization, utilizing a channel-based architecture with isolated notebooks for servers and non-server channels, while maintaining shared agent identities across channels via CLAUDE.md files","zh":"赋予代理重新组织其现有设置以形成具有服务器和非服务器通道隔离笔记本的基于通道的架构，同时通过CLAUDE.md文件在通道间保持共享的代理身份","ja":"エージェントがサーバーと非サーバーチャネルの隔離ノートブックを備えたチャネルベースのアーキテクチャに既存の設定を再構成できるようにし、CLAUDE.mdファイルを介してチャネル間で共有されるエージェントIDを維持","ko":"에이전트가 서버와 비서버 채널용 분리 노트북을 갖춘 채널 기반 아키텍처로 기존 설정을 재구성할 수 있도록 하며, CLAUDE.md 파일을 통해 채널 간에 공유되는 에이전트 ID를 유지","es":"Habilita a los agentes a reestructurar su configuración existente en una organización jerárquica, utilizando una arquitectura basada en canales con cuadernos aislados para servidores y canales no servidores, mientras mantiene identidades de agentes compartidas en todos los canales a través de archivos CLAUDE.md","fr":"Permet aux agents de restructurer leur configuration existante en une organisation hiérarchique, en utilisant une architecture basée sur les canaux avec des cahiers isolés pour les serveurs et les canaux non serveurs, tout en maintenant des identités d''agents partagées sur tous les canaux via des fichiers CLAUDE.md","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, ihre bestehende Konfiguration in eine hierarchische Organisation umzustrukturieren, indem sie eine kanalbasierte Architektur mit isolierten Notizbüchern für Server und nicht-Server-Kanäle verwenden, während sie gemeinsame Agenten-Identitäten über alle Kanäle hinweg über CLAUDE.md-Dateien beibehalten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reestruturar sua configuração existente em uma organização hierárquica, utilizando uma arquitetura baseada em canais com cadernos isolados para servidores e canais não servidores, mantendo identidades de agentes compartilhadas entre canais via arquivos CLAUDE.md","ru":"Позволяет агентам перестроить свою существующую настройку в иерархическую организацию, используя архитектуру на основе каналов с изолированными блокнотами для серверов и не-серверных каналов, сохраняя общие идентификаторы агентов между каналами через файлы CLAUDE.md","ar":"تمكّن العمال من إعادة هيكلة إعداداتهم الحالية في منظمة هرمية، باستخدام هندسة قائمة على القنوات مع دفاتر منفصلة للخادمات والقنوات غير الخادمات، مع الحفاظ على هويات العمال المشتركة عبر القنوات من خلال ملفات CLAUDE.md"},"useCases":{"en":["Migrating existing group chats to channel-based workspaces","Organizing server and category teams into isolated notebooks","Integrating non-server channels like WhatsApp and Telegram into the new architecture"],"zh":["将现有群聊迁移到基于通道的工作空间","将服务器和类别团队组织到隔离的笔记本中","将非服务器通道（如WhatsApp和Telegram）集成到新架构中"],"ja":["既存のグループチャットをチャネルベースのワークスペースに移行","サーバーとカテゴリーチームを隔離されたノートブックに組織","非サーバーチャネル（例：WhatsApp、Telegram）を新しいアーキテクチャに統合"],"ko":["기존 그룹 채팅을 채널 기반 작업 공간으로 마이그레이션","서버 및 카테고리 팀을 분리된 노트북으로 구성","비서버 채널(예: WhatsApp, Telegram)을 새로운 아키텍처에 통합"],"es":["Migrar chats de grupo existentes a espacios de trabajo basados en canales","Organizar equipos de servidores y categorías en cuadernos aislados","Integrar canales no servidores como WhatsApp y Telegram en la nueva arquitectura"],"fr":["Migrer des conversations de groupe existantes vers des espaces de travail basés sur les canaux","Organiser des équipes de serveurs et de catégories en cahiers isolés","Intégrer des canaux non serveurs comme WhatsApp et Telegram dans la nouvelle architecture"],"de":["Migrieren von bestehenden Gruppenchats in kanalbasierte Arbeitsbereiche","Organisieren von Server- und Kategorieteams in isolierte Notizbücher","Integrieren von nicht-Server-Kanälen wie WhatsApp und Telegram in die neue Architektur"],"pt":["Migrar conversas de grupo existentes para espaços de trabalho baseados em canais","Organizar equipes de servidores e categorias em cadernos isolados","Integrar canais não servidores como WhatsApp e Telegram na nova arquitetura"],"ru":["Перенос существующих групповых чатов в рабочие пространства на основе каналов","Организация команд серверов и категорий в изолированные блокноты","Интеграция не-серверных каналов, таких как WhatsApp и Telegram, в новую архитектуру"],"ar":["نقل محادثات المجموعة الحالية إلى مساحات عمل قائمة على القنوات","تنظيم فرق الخادمات والفئات في دفاتر منفصلة","دمج قنوات غير خادمات مثل WhatsApp وTelegram في الهندسة الجديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing OmniClaw setup","Limited to migrating to the specified layered context architecture"],"zh":["需要现有的OmniClaw设置","仅限于迁移到指定的分层上下文架构"],"ja":["既存のOmniClaw設定が必要","指定された階層化されたコンテキストアーキテクチャへの移行のみ"],"ko":["기존 OmniClaw 설정이 필요","지정된 계층화된 컨텍스트 아키텍처로의 마이그레이션만 지원"],"es":["Requiere una configuración existente de OmniClaw","Limitado a la migración a la arquitectura de contexto en capas especificada"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration existante d''OmniClaw","Limité à la migration vers l''architecture de contexte en couches spécifiée"],"de":["Benötigt eine bestehende OmniClaw-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf die Migration zur angegebenen schichtbasierten Kontextarchitektur"],"pt":["Exige configuração OmniClaw existente","Limitado à migração para a arquitetura de contexto em camadas especificada"],"ru":["Требует существующей настройки OmniClaw","Ограничен переносом в указанную архитектуру контекста в слоях"],"ar":["يتطلب إعدادات OmniClaw الحالية","محدود بنقل إلى هندسة سياق متعددة الطبقات المحددة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c4ec350aa88665b722bd65195cb40ba14a29cb2fe8fc6bbd9b82d49d752d31ba","qualityScore":37}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ferrucc-io/clog/reproduce', 'community', 'ferrucc-io', 'clog', 'ferrucc-io/clog', 'reproduce', 2, 0, 37, '2026-02-27T20:02:30Z', '2026-02-28T01:38:41.799Z', 'd452ac7c230fd9e1b40a2097334b8ea8599a1f7c1129cdebc8ce8115a1663bb1', '{"id":"ferrucc-io/clog/reproduce","name":"reproduce","description":{"zh":"reproduce是一种CLI + Skill，用于与Claude Code一起进行调试，提高开发效率","ja":"reproduceは、Claude Codeとともにデバッグを行うためのCLI + スキルで、開発効率を向上","ko":"reproduce는 Claude Code와 함께 디버깅을 수행하는 CLI + 스킬로 개발 효율성을 높입니다","es":"Reproduce es una herramienta de línea de comandos (CLI) para depuración con Claude Code, diseñada para desarrolladores","fr":"Reproduce est un outil en ligne de commande (CLI) pour le débogage avec Claude Code, conçu pour les développeurs","de":"Reproduce ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool (CLI) für das Debugging mit Claude Code, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"O skill de reprodução é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para depurar com Claude Code, permitindo que os desenvolvedores resolvam problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык воспроизведения - это инструмент командной строки для отладки с Claude Code, позволяющий разработчикам эффективно решать проблемы","ar":"مهارة إعادة الإنتاج هي أداة سطر أوامر لتصحيح الأخطاء مع Claude Code، مما يسمح للمطورين بحل المشكلات بفعالية","en":"A CLI + Skill for debugging with Claude Code"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI工具：reproduce 调试CLI技能","ja":"AIエージェント：reproduce デバッグCLIスキル","ko":"AI 에이전트: reproduce 디버깅 CLI 스킬","es":"Herramientas de AI: Reproduce CLI para Depuración","fr":"Outils d''IA: Reproduce CLI pour le Débogage","de":"KI-Tools: Reproduce CLI für Debugging","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: Reproduzir com Claude Code","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Reproduce с Claude Code","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: إعادة إنتاج مع Claude Code","en":"reproduce"},"description":{"zh":"reproduce是一种CLI + Skill，用于与Claude Code一起进行调试，提高开发效率","ja":"reproduceは、Claude Codeとともにデバッグを行うためのCLI + スキルで、開発効率を向上","ko":"reproduce는 Claude Code와 함께 디버깅을 수행하는 CLI + 스킬로 개발 효율성을 높입니다","es":"Reproduce es una herramienta de línea de comandos (CLI) para depuración con Claude Code, diseñada para desarrolladores","fr":"Reproduce est un outil en ligne de commande (CLI) pour le débogage avec Claude Code, conçu pour les développeurs","de":"Reproduce ist ein Kommandozeilen-Tool (CLI) für das Debugging mit Claude Code, entwickelt für Entwickler","pt":"O skill de reprodução é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para depurar com Claude Code, permitindo que os desenvolvedores resolvam problemas de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык воспроизведения - это инструмент командной строки для отладки с Claude Code, позволяющий разработчикам эффективно решать проблемы","ar":"مهارة إعادة الإنتاج هي أداة سطر أوامر لتصحيح الأخطاء مع Claude Code، مما يسمح للمطورين بحل المشكلات بفعالية","en":"A CLI + Skill for debugging with Claude Code"},"definition":{"en":"A CLI + Skill for debugging with Claude Code"},"features":{"zh":["CLI接口","与Claude Code集成","提高调试效率","支持多种开发语言","简化开发流程"],"ja":["CLIインターフェース","Claude Codeとの統合","デバッグ効率の向上","複数の開発言語をサポート","開発プロセスの簡素化"],"ko":["CLI 인터페이스","Claude Code와의 통합","디버깅 효율성 향상","다중 개발 언어 지원","개발 프로세스 간소화"],"es":["Depuración con Claude Code","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI)","Herramienta de AI para desarrolladores","Mejora de habilidades de depuración","Integración con Claude Code"],"fr":["Débogage avec Claude Code","Interface en ligne de commande (CLI)","Outil d''IA pour les développeurs","Amélioration des compétences en débogage","Intégration avec Claude Code"],"de":["Debugging mit Claude Code","Kommandozeilen-Interface (CLI)","KI-Tool für Entwickler","Verbesserung der Fähigkeiten im Debugging","Integration mit Claude Code"],"pt":["Depuração com Claude Code","Ferramenta de linha de comando","Resolução eficiente de problemas","Integração com CLI","Suporte a desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Отладка с Claude Code","Инструмент командной строки","Эффективное решение проблем","Интеграция с CLI","Поддержка разработчиков"],"ar":["تصحيح الأخطاء مع Claude Code","أداة سطر أوامر","حل فعال للمشكلات","التكامل مع CLI","دعم المطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","reproduce安装","CLI调试","Claude Code教程","如何使用reproduce","reproduce替代品","reproduce与其他工具的比较","开发效率提高","调试技巧"],"ja":["AIエージェント","reproduceのインストール","CLIデバッグ","Claude Codeのチュートリアル","reproduceの使い方","reproduceの代替","reproduceと他のツールの比較","開発効率の向上","デバッグテクニック"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","reproduce 설치","CLI 디버깅","Claude Code 튜토리얼","reproduce 사용법","reproduce 대체","reproduce와 다른 툴의 비교","개발 효율성 향상","디버깅 기술"],"es":["herramientas de AI","depuración con Claude Code","reproduce CLI","cómo usar reproduce","alternativas a reproduce","reproduce vs otros depuradores","instalación de reproduce","guía de configuración de reproduce"],"fr":["outils d''IA","débogage avec Claude Code","reproduce CLI","comment utiliser reproduce","alternatives à reproduce","reproduce vs autres débogueurs","installation de reproduce","guide de configuration de reproduce"],"de":["KI-Tools","Debugging mit Claude Code","reproduce CLI","wie man reproduce verwendet","alternativen zu reproduce","reproduce vs andere debugger","installation von reproduce","konfigurationsanleitung für reproduce"],"pt":["como usar o skill de reprodução","o que é o skill de reprodução","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","alternativas ao claude code","claude code vs outros","instalar o skill de reprodução","guia de configuração do skill de reprodução"],"ru":["как использовать навык воспроизведения","что такое навык воспроизведения","инструменты ии для разработчиков","альтернативы claude code","claude code vs другие","установить навык воспроизведения","руководство по настройке навыка воспроизведения"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام مهارة إعادة الإنتاج","ما هي مهارة إعادة الإنتاج","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","بديلات كلود كود","كلود كود مقابل غيره","تثبيت مهارة إعادة الإنتاج","دليل إعداد مهارة إعادة الإنتاج"]}},"owner":"ferrucc-io","repo":"clog","repoPath":"ferrucc-io/clog","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T20:02:30Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"reproduce","description":"Debug a users bug by instrumenting their code with clog log statements, having them reproduce the issue, then analyzing the logs to find root cause","bodyPreview":"# Debug with clog\n\nYou are a debugging assistant. You use `clog` — a local log ingestion CLI — to help the user find the root cause of a bug. The workflow is: instrument code with log statements that POST to clog, have the user reproduce the bug, then analyze the captured logs.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore starting, make sure the clog server is running:\n\n```bash\nclog status\n```\n\nIf it''s not running, start it:\n\n```bash\nclog start\n```\n\nIf `clog` is not installed, tell the user to install it:\n```\ncarg","body":"# Debug with clog\n\nYou are a debugging assistant. You use `clog` — a local log ingestion CLI — to help the user find the root cause of a bug. The workflow is: instrument code with log statements that POST to clog, have the user reproduce the bug, then analyze the captured logs.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore starting, make sure the clog server is running:\n\n```bash\nclog status\n```\n\nIf it''s not running, start it:\n\n```bash\nclog start\n```\n\nIf `clog` is not installed, tell the user to install it:\n```\ncargo install --path <path-to-clog-repo>\n```\n\nThe clog server always runs on port **2999**.\n\n## Step 1: Understand the bug\n\nAsk the user:\n- What is the bug? What''s the expected vs actual behavior?\n- Where in the codebase do they think the problem is? (file, function, flow)\n- How do they reproduce it?\n\nIf the user already described the bug (e.g. as an argument to `/debug`), skip straight to investigating the relevant code area. Use `$ARGUMENTS` as the bug description if provided.\n\n## Step 2: Instrument the code\n\nRead the relevant source files and add logging statements that POST JSON to clog. Choose the right language for the user''s codebase:\n\n**Python:**\n```python\nimport urllib.request, json\ndef _clog(data):\n    try:\n        urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(\n            \"http://localhost:2999/log\",\n            data=json.dumps(data).encode(),\n            headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n            method=\"POST\"))\n    except: pass\n```\n\n**JavaScript/TypeScript (Node):**\n```javascript\nfunction _clog(data) {\n  fetch(\"http://localhost:2999/log\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify(data),\n  }).catch(() => {});\n}\n```\n\n**Rust:**\n```rust\nfn _clog(data: &impl serde::Serialize) {\n    let _ = reqwest::blocking::Client::new()\n        .post(\"http://localhost:2999/log\")\n        .json(data)\n        .send();\n}\n```\n\n**Shell/curl:**\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:2999/log \\\n  -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' \\\n  -d ''{\"step\":\"description\",\"value\":\"...\"}''\n```\n\n### What to log\n\nPlace log statements at key points in the suspected code path:\n- Function entry/exit with argument values\n- Branch decisions (which `if`/`else`/`match` arm was taken)\n- Variable values before and after transformations\n- Loop iterations with index and relevant state\n- Error catch blocks with the error details\n- API request/response payloads\n\nEach log payload should include a `\"step\"` field describing where in the flow it is, plus whatever data is relevant. Example:\n\n```python\n_clog({\"step\": \"validate_input\", \"user_id\": user_id, \"payload\": payload})\n_clog({\"step\": \"db_query_result\", \"rows\": len(rows), \"first\": rows[0] if rows else None})\n_clog({\"step\": \"transform_output\", \"before\": raw, \"after\": transformed})\n```\n\nKeep log statements minimal and non-invasive — they should not change control flow.\n\n## Step 3: Ask the user to reproduce\n\nOnce instrumentation is in place, tell the user:\n\n> I''ve added debug logging to the code. Please reproduce the bug now — do exactly what triggers the issue. Let me know when you''re done.\n\nWait for the user to confirm they''ve reproduced the bug before proceeding.\n\n## Step 4: Analyze the logs\n\nClear any old logs first if you started fresh, otherwise look at recent entries:\n\n```bash\nclog latest -n 50\n```\n\nFor targeted searches, use grep on the log file directly:\n\n```bash\ngrep \"step\" ~/.clog/logs/clog.ndjson\n```\n\nOr use `clog latest` with a filter:\n\n```bash\nclog latest -n 100 -q \"error\"\nclog latest -n 100 -q \"step_name\"\n```\n\nFor more powerful searches, use ripgrep:\n\n```bash\nrg \"pattern\" ~/.clog/logs/clog.ndjson\n```\n\n### Analysis approach\n\n1. **Trace the flow** — read logs chronologically to see what path the code took\n2. **Find the divergence** — identify where actual behavior deviated from expected\n3. **Inspect values** — look at variable states at the divergence point\n4. **Check for missing logs** — if an expected log step is absent, that code path wasn''t reached\n5. **Correlate timestamps** — use the `ts` field to identify timing issues or ordering problems\n\n## Step 5: Report findings and fix\n\nOnce you''ve identified the root cause:\n\n1. Explain to the user what you found, referencing specific log entries\n2. Propose a fix\n3. Remove all the `_clog` instrumentation you added (the logging was temporary)\n4. Clean up: `clog clear`\n\n## Important notes\n\n- Always remove instrumentation after debugging. The `_clog` calls are not production code.\n- If the first round of logs isn''t enough, add more targeted instrumentation and ask the user to reproduce again.\n- If `clog status` shows the server is dead mid-session, restart it with `clog start`.\n- The log file is at `~/.clog/logs/clog.ndjson` — each line is `{\"ts\":\"...\",\"data\":{...}}`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T01:38:41.799Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Debugging Agents requiring real-time log analysis and root cause identification.","zh":"非常适合需要实时日志分析和根本原因识别的调试代理。","ja":"リアルタイムのログ分析と根本原因の特定を必要とするデバッグエージェントに最適です。","ko":"실시간 로그 분석 및 근본 원인 식별이 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para depurar Agents que requieren análisis de logs en tiempo real e identificación de la causa raíz.","fr":"Idéal pour le débogage d''Agents nécessitant une analyse de logs en temps réel et une identification de la cause racine.","de":"Ideal zum Debuggen von Agents, die Echtzeit-Log-Analyse und die Identifizierung der Ursache erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Depuração que requerem análise de logs em tempo real e identificação da causa raiz.","ru":"Идеально подходит для отладочных агентов, требующих анализа журналов в реальном времени и определения первопричины.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التصحيح الذين يتطلبون تحليل السجلات في الوقت الفعلي وتحديد السبب الجذري."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to analyze runtime behavior through captured log streams from clog instrumentation. Provides direct access to structured debugging data via local HTTP POST endpoints for precise bug reproduction scenarios.","zh":"通过从 clog 检测捕获的日志流，使代理能够分析运行时行为。通过本地 HTTP POST 端点提供对结构化调试数据的直接访问，以实现精确的错误复现场景。","ja":"clog インストルメンテーションからキャプチャされたログストリームを通じて、エージェントがランタイム動作を分析できるようにします。正確なバグ再現シナリオのために、ローカル HTTP POST エンドポイントを介して構造化されたデバッグデータへの直接アクセスを提供します。","ko":"clog 인스트루멘테이션에서 캡처한 로그 스트림을 통해 에이전트가 런타임 동작을 분석할 수 있도록 합니다. 정확한 버그 재현 시나리오를 위해 로컬 HTTP POST 엔드포인트를 통해 구조화된 디버깅 데이터에 대한 직접 액세스를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agents analizar el comportamiento en tiempo de ejecución mediante flujos de logs capturados de la instrumentación clog. Proporciona acceso directo a datos de depuración estructurados a través de endpoints HTTP POST locales para escenarios precisos de reproducción de errores.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser le comportement d''exécution via des flux de logs capturés provenant de l''instrumentation clog. Fournit un accès direct aux données de débogage structurées via des endpoints HTTP POST locaux pour des scénarios de reproduction de bugs précis.","de":"Ermöglicht Agents, das Laufzeitverhalten durch erfasste Log-Streams von clog-Instrumentierung zu analysieren. Bietet direkten Zugriff auf strukturierte Debug-Daten über lokale HTTP POST Endpoints für präzise Bug-Reproduktionsszenarien.","pt":"Permite que os agentes analisem o comportamento em tempo de execução por meio de fluxos de logs capturados da instrumentação clog. Fornece acesso direto a dados estruturados de depuração via endpoints locais HTTP POST para cenários precisos de reprodução de bugs.","ru":"Позволяет агентам анализировать поведение во время выполнения через захваченные потоки журналов из инструментирования clog. Обеспечивает прямой доступ к структурированным отладочным данным через локальные конечные точки HTTP POST для точных сценариев воспроизведения ошибок.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تحليل سلوك وقت التشغيل من خلال تدفقات السجلات التي تم التقاطها من أداة clog. يوفر وصولاً مباشراً إلى بيانات التصحيح المنظمة عبر نقاط نهاية HTTP POST المحلية لحالات استنساخ الأخطاء بدقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing runtime execution flows","Identifying root causes from instrumented logs","Reproducing bugs through captured log sequences","Debugging with structured log ingestion"],"zh":["分析运行时执行流","从检测日志中识别根本原因","通过捕获的日志序列重现错误","通过结构化日志摄取进行调试"],"ja":["ランタイム実行フローの分析","インストルメント化されたログからの根本原因の特定","キャプチャされたログシーケンスによるバグの再現","構造化ログインジェスションによるデバッグ"],"ko":["런타임 실행 흐름 분석","인스트루멘트화된 로그에서 근본 원인 식별","캡처된 로그 시퀀스를 통한 버그 재현","구조화된 로그 수집을 통한 디버깅"],"es":["Analizar flujos de ejecución en tiempo de ejecución","Identificar causas raíz a partir de logs instrumentados","Reproducir errores mediante secuencias de logs capturadas","Depurar con ingesta de logs estructurados"],"fr":["Analyser les flux d''exécution en temps d''exécution","Identifier les causes racines à partir de logs instrumentés","Reproduire les bugs via des séquences de logs capturées","Déboguer avec l''ingestion de logs structurés"],"de":["Analysieren von Laufzeitausführungsflüssen","Identifizieren von Ursachen aus instrumentierten Logs","Reproduzieren von Bugs durch erfasste Log-Sequenzen","Debuggen mit strukturierter Log-Erfassung"],"pt":["Analisando fluxos de execução em tempo de execução","Identificando causas raiz a partir de logs instrumentados","Reproduzindo bugs por meio de sequências de logs capturadas","Depurando com ingestão estruturada de logs"],"ru":["Анализ потоков выполнения во время выполнения","Определение первопричин из инструментированных журналов","Воспроизведение ошибок через захваченные последовательности журналов","Отладка со структурированным приемом журналов"],"ar":["تحليل تدفقات تنفيذ وقت التشغيل","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية من السجلات المؤداة","استنساخ الأخطاء من خلال تسلسلات السجلات التي تم التقاطها","التصحيح مع تناول منظم للسجلات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clog server running locally","Needs code instrumentation with POST statements","Dependent on user reproducing the bug","Requires clog CLI installation"],"zh":["需要在本地运行 clog 服务器","需要使用 POST 语句进行代码检测","依赖于用户重现错误","需要安装 clog CLI"],"ja":["ローカルで実行されている clog サーバーが必要","POST ステートメントを使用したコードインストルメンテーションが必要","ユーザーによるバグの再現に依存","clog CLI のインストールが必要"],"ko":["로컬에서 실행 중인 clog 서버 필요","POST 문을 사용한 코드 인스트루멘테이션 필요","사용자가 버그를 재현해야 함","clog CLI 설치 필요"],"es":["Requiere que el servidor clog esté ejecutándose localmente","Necesita instrumentación de código con declaraciones POST","Depende de que el usuario reproduzca el error","Requiere la instalación de clog CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite que le serveur clog soit exécuté localement","Nécessite une instrumentation du code avec des instructions POST","Dépend de la reproduction du bug par l''utilisateur","Nécessite l''installation de clog CLI"],"de":["Erfordert, dass der clog-Server lokal läuft","Benötigt Code-Instrumentierung mit POST-Anweisungen","Abhängig davon, dass der Benutzer den Bug reproduziert","Erfordert die Installation der clog CLI"],"pt":["Requer que o servidor clog esteja em execução localmente","Necessita de instrumentação de código com instruções POST","Dependente do usuário reproduzir o bug","Requer instalação do CLI clog"],"ru":["Требует локально запущенного сервера clog","Требует инструментирования кода с операторами POST","Зависит от пользователя, воспроизводящего ошибку","Требует установки CLI clog"],"ar":["يتطلب تشغيل خادم clog محلياً","يحتاج إلى أداة تعليم البرمجة بجمل POST","يعتمد على المستخدم لإعادة إنتاج الخطأ","يتطلب تثبيت CLI clog"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d452ac7c230fd9e1b40a2097334b8ea8599a1f7c1129cdebc8ce8115a1663bb1","qualityScore":37}');
