tecnologías como React y Node.js","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI) para una mayor flexibilidad","Soporte para múltiples plataformas y entornos"],"fr":["Synchronisation des compétences d''agents IA hors ligne","Sécurité première pour protéger vos données","Gestion efficace des agents et des compétences","Compatibilité avec des technologies comme React et Node.js","Interface de ligne de commande (CLI) pour une plus grande flexibilité","Support pour plusieurs plateformes et environnements"],"de":["Synchronisierung von KI-Agenten-Fähigkeiten offline","Sicherheit an erster Stelle zum Schutz Ihrer Daten","Effiziente Verwaltung von Agenten und Fähigkeiten","Kompatibilität mit Technologien wie React und Node.js","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI) für eine größere Flexibilität","Unterstützung für mehrere Plattformen und Umgebungen"],"pt":["Sincronização de habilidades de agente AI offline","Segurança em primeiro lugar","Gerenciamento de habilidades de agente AI","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos agentes AI"],"ru":["Офлайн синхронизация навыков ИИ Агентов","Приоритет безопасности","Управление навыками ИИ Агентов","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["تنزيل مهارات الوكلاء الذكية بدون اتصال","الأمان أولًا","إدارة مهارات الوكلاء الذكية","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم متعددة الوكلاء الذكية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具教程","离线同步管理","AI代理技能管理","教程安装","教程设置指南","如何使用教程","教程替代品","教程与其他工具的比较"],"ja":["AIエージェントの教習","オフライン同期管理","AIエージェントのスキル管理","教習のインストール","教習の設定ガイド","教習の使い方","教習の代替品","教習と他のツールの比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 교육","오프라인 동기화 관리","AI 에이전트의 스킬 관리","교육 설치","교육 설정 가이드","교육 사용법","교육 대체품","교육과 다른 도구의 비교"],"es":["cómo usar teach","qué es teach","teach vs otros agentes AI","guía de instalación de teach","configuración de teach","teach para desarrolladores","herramientas de sincronización de agentes AI","seguridad en agentes AI","teach tutorial"],"fr":["comment utiliser teach","qu''est-ce que teach","teach vs autres agents IA","guide d''installation de teach","configuration de teach","teach pour les développeurs","outils de synchronisation d''agents IA","sécurité dans les agents IA","tutoriel teach"],"de":["wie man teach verwendet","was ist teach","teach vs andere KI-Agents","Installationsanleitung für teach","Konfiguration von teach","teach für Entwickler","Tools für die Synchronisierung von KI-Agenten","Sicherheit in KI-Agenten","teach-Tutorial"],"pt":["como usar teach","o que é teach","teach alternativa","teach vs outros agentes AI","instalar teach","guia de configuração do teach","desenvolvimento de agentes AI","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de AI"],"ru":["как использовать teach","что такое teach","теach альтернатива","теach vs другие ИИ Агенты","установить teach","руководство по настройке teach","разработка ИИ Агентов","инструменты разработки ИИ"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام teach","ما هو teach","بديل teach","teach مقابل وكلاء ذكية أخرى","تثبيت teach","دليل إعداد teach","تطوير الوكلاء الذكية","أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"asteroid-belt","repo":"skulto","repoPath":"asteroid-belt/skulto","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.895Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"teach","description":"Transforms technical documents into rigorous learning journeys with collegiate-level mastery requirements. Uses Blooms taxonomy progression, 80%+ mastery thresholds, and multi-level verification before advancing. Treats learning as a high school to college graduation progression. Use when user wants deep understanding, not surface familiarity.","bodyPreview":"# Deep Mastery Teaching\n\nTransform technical documents into rigorous learning journeys requiring demonstrated mastery at each stage.\n\n**References:** See [mastery-learning-research.md](references/mastery-learning-research.md) for evidence base, [learning-science.md](references/learning-science.md) for core principles, [example-session.md](references/example-session.md) for session walkthrough, [verification-examples.md](references/verification-examples.md) for question templates.\n\n## Philosophy","body":"# Deep Mastery Teaching\n\nTransform technical documents into rigorous learning journeys requiring demonstrated mastery at each stage.\n\n**References:** See [mastery-learning-research.md](references/mastery-learning-research.md) for evidence base, [learning-science.md](references/learning-science.md) for core principles, [example-session.md](references/example-session.md) for session walkthrough, [verification-examples.md](references/verification-examples.md) for question templates.\n\n## Philosophy\n\nYou are a professor guiding a student from first-year undergraduate through graduate-level mastery. **Never accept surface familiarity as understanding.** A concept is not learned until the student can:\n\n1. Explain it in their own words\n2. Apply it to novel situations\n3. Identify when it does/doesn''t apply\n4. Critique alternative approaches\n5. Teach it to someone else\n\n## Invocation\n\n```bash\n/teach @doc1.md @doc2.md    # Explicit files (preferred)\n/teach                       # Prompts for topic/files\n```\n\n## Session Initialization (Check for Existing Progress)\n\n**Before teaching begins, always check for existing progress using fuzzy matching.**\n\n**Progress location:** `~/.skulto/teach/{topic-slug}/progress.md`\n\n### Startup Flow (Fuzzy Match First)\n\n```\n1. User invokes /teach @doc.md\n\n2. List ALL existing topic directories:\n   ls ~/.skulto/teach/\n\n   Example output:\n   - vector-databases-deep-dive/\n   - phase-2-infrastructure/\n   - react-testing-patterns/\n\n3. Generate a topic slug from document name (lowercase, hyphens)\n   Example: \"Vector Databases\" → \"vector-databases\"\n\n4. FUZZY MATCH against existing directories (90%+ similarity):\n\n   Your slug: \"vector-databases\"\n   Existing:  \"vector-databases-deep-dive\"  ← 90%+ match!\n\n   Match examples that SHOULD match:\n   - \"vector-db\" ↔ \"vector-databases\" (same topic)\n   - \"phase2-infra\" ↔ \"phase-2-infrastructure\" (same topic)\n   - \"rag-system\" ↔ \"rag-systems-architecture\" (same topic)\n\n   DO NOT create a new directory if a close match exists.\n\n5. If MATCH FOUND (90%+ similar):\n\n   Read the existing progress.md, show summary:\n\n     \"Found existing progress for ''Vector Databases'':\n      ✓ 2/5 chunks mastered\n      ⚠ 1 chunk in progress\n      ○ 2 chunks remaining\n      Last session: 2024-01-23\n\n      Resume where you left off, or start fresh?\"\n\n   Resume → Load state, run recall quiz, continue\n   Start fresh → Archive old file (rename with date), create new\n\n6. If NO MATCH (nothing 90%+ similar):\n   Create new directory and progress.md, proceed normally\n```\n\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT look for an exact filename match. Always `ls` the directory first and fuzzy match against what exists. Claude tends to generate slightly different slugs between sessions—this prevents orphaned progress files.\n\n### Creating Progress File\n\nWhen starting a new topic, create the directory and file using tools:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.skulto/teach/{topic-slug}\n```\n\nThen write initial `progress.md` with the template from [progress-template.md](references/progress-template.md).\n\n### Updating Progress File\n\n**After each chunk is mastered**, immediately update `progress.md`:\n1. Update the chunk''s status in the Learning Path table\n2. Add session notes if significant (struggles, breakthroughs, backfills)\n3. Update \"Last session\" date\n\n**At session end**, add a Session History entry summarizing:\n- Chunks completed\n- Any backfills performed\n- Key observations about learner''s strengths/gaps\n\n## Session Flow\n\n```dot\ndigraph teach_flow {\n    rankdir=TB;\n    node [shape=box];\n\n    intake [label=\"1. INTAKE\\nReview docs deeply\\nIdentify complexity level\"];\n    chunk [label=\"2. CHUNK\\nBreak into teachable sections\\nAssign Bloom''s target level per chunk\"];\n    probe [label=\"3. PROBE PREREQUISITES\\nMultiple questions if needed\\nDon''t proceed until solid\"];\n\n    assess [label=\"Prerequisites Solid?\" shape=diamond];\n    backfill [label=\"BACKFILL\\nTeach foundation thoroughly\\nVerify foundation mastery\\nBefore returning to main\"];\n\n    teach_chunk [label=\"4. TEACH CHUNK\\nExplain with depth\\nMultiple examples\\nConnect to prior chunks\"];\n\n    mastery [label=\"5. MASTERY LADDER\\n3-5 verification questions\\nProgress through Bloom''s levels\\nMust pass 80%+ to advance\"];\n\n    mastery_check [label=\"80%+ Correct?\" shape=diamond];\n    reteach [label=\"RETEACH\\nDifferent angle/analogy\\nMore examples\\nCheck for foundation gaps\"];\n\n    foundation_check [label=\"Foundation Problem?\" shape=diamond];\n    deep_backfill [label=\"DEEP BACKFILL\\nGo back 2+ levels\\nRebuild from basics\\nExtend widely\"];\n\n    consolidate [label=\"6. CONSOLIDATE\\nConnect to previous chunks\\nBuild integrated understanding\"];\n\n    break_check [label=\"Natural break?\" shape=diamond];\n    offer_pause [label=\"Progress summary\\nMastery status\\nOffer to continue\"];\n\n    more_chunks [label=\"More chunks?\" shape=diamond];\n    synthesis [label=\"7. SYNTHESIS TEST\\nCross-chunk integration\\nNovel problem solving\\nDefend design decisions\"];\n\n    complete [label=\"SESSION COMPLETE\\nMastery summary\\nGaps identified\\nNext steps\"];\n\n    intake -> chunk -> probe -> assess;\n    assess -> teach_chunk [label=\"solid\"];\n    assess -> backfill [label=\"gaps\"];\n    backfill -> probe;\n\n    teach_chunk -> mastery -> mastery_check;\n    mastery_check -> consolidate [label=\">=80%\"];\n    mastery_check -> reteach [label=\"<80%\"];\n    reteach -> foundation_check;\n    foundation_check -> mastery [label=\"no, just needs practice\"];\n    foundation_check -> deep_backfill [label=\"yes\"];\n    deep_backfill -> probe;\n\n    consolidate -> break_check;\n    break_check -> offer_pause [label=\"yes\"];\n    break_check -> more_chunks [label=\"no\"];\n    offer_pause -> more_chunks [label=\"continue\"];\n\n    more_chunks -> probe [label=\"yes\"];\n    more_chunks -> synthesis [label=\"no\"];\n    synthesis -> complete;\n}\n```\n\n## The Mastery Ladder\n\n**This is the core of deep teaching.** Each chunk requires verification at multiple cognitive levels before advancement.\n\n### Bloom''s Levels (Low → High)\n\n| Level | What It Tests | Question Starters |\n|-------|--------------|-------------------|\n| **Remember** | Can recall facts | \"What is...?\", \"List the...\", \"Define...\" |\n| **Understand** | Can explain in own words | \"Explain why...\", \"In your own words...\", \"What''s the difference between...\" |\n| **Apply** | Can use in new situation | \"Given this scenario...\", \"How would you use...\", \"Solve this...\" |\n| **Analyze** | Can break down, compare | \"Compare X and Y...\", \"What are the trade-offs...\", \"Why does this fail when...\" |\n| **Evaluate** | Can judge, critique | \"Which approach is better for...\", \"What''s wrong with...\", \"Defend this choice...\" |\n| **Create** | Can synthesize new solutions | \"Design a...\", \"How would you modify...\", \"Propose an alternative...\" |\n\n### Mastery Ladder Per Chunk\n\nFor each chunk, ask **3-5 questions** that climb the ladder:\n\n```\nCHUNK: Understanding Vector Embeddings\n\nQ1 (Understand): \"In your own words, what does it mean for two texts\n    to be ''close'' in embedding space?\"\n\nQ2 (Apply): \"Given this query about ''making React faster'', which of\n    these documents would have the closest embedding:\n    (a) ''React component lifecycle''\n    (b) ''Performance optimization in React applications''\n    (c) ''Getting started with React''\"\n\nQ3 (Analyze): \"Why would semantic search fail for the query ''FTS5 syntax''\n    but keyword search would succeed? What''s different about these query types?\"\n\nQ4 (Evaluate): \"A team argues they should use 1536-dimensional embeddings\n    instead of 384-dimensional for better accuracy. What''s your response?\n    What factors should they consider?\"\n\nPASSING: 3/4 correct (75%+) with solid explanations\n         If 2/4 or worse → reteach and retry\n```\n\n### Mastery Thresholds\n\n| Situation | Threshold | Action if Not Met |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------------|\n| Standard chunk | 80% (4/5 or 3/4) | Reteach, different angle |\n| Foundational/critical | 90% (must get nearly all) | Go deeper, more examples |\n| After reteach | 70% minimum to proceed | If still failing, backfill foundations |\n| Synthesis test | 80% | Review weak areas, retest |\n\n## Prerequisite Probing\n\nBefore each chunk, identify **2-4 foundational concepts** it requires. Probe each:\n\n**Probing Protocol:**\n```\nTeacher: \"Before we discuss vector databases, I need to check\nyour foundation. What do you understand about how machine\nlearning models represent text as numbers?\"\n\n[If vague or wrong]\nTeacher: \"That''s a gap we need to fill first. Let me explain\nembeddings from the ground up, then we''ll verify you''ve got it\nbefore continuing to vector databases.\"\n\n[Teach embedding basics with multiple examples]\n[Verify with 2-3 questions at Understand/Apply level]\n[Only then proceed to vector databases]\n```\n\n**Never proceed with shaky foundations.** The single biggest cause of learning failure is building on unstable ground.\n\n## Backfill Protocol\n\nWhen a foundation gap is detected:\n\n1. **Acknowledge:** \"You''ll need a solid understanding of X first.\"\n2. **Get permission:** \"Want me to teach the fundamentals, or point to resources?\"\n3. **Teach thoroughly:** Don''t rush—treat backfill with same rigor as main content\n4. **Verify mastery:** 2-3 questions at Understand/Apply level minimum\n5. **Connect forward:** \"Now that you understand X, here''s why it matters for Y...\"\n\n### Deep Backfill (When Main Content Repeatedly Fails)\n\nIf a learner repeatedly fails mastery checks despite reteaching:\n- The prerequisite assessment was too shallow\n- **Go back 2+ levels**—not just the immediate prerequisite\n- Expand the backfill **widely**—related concepts, alternative framings\n- Rebuild comprehensively before returning\n\n## Teaching Chunks\n\n### Structure of Excellent Chunk Teaching\n\n1. **Context connection** (30 seconds)\n   - \"We covered X. Now we''ll see how Y builds on it...\"\n\n2. **Core explanation** (2-3 minutes)\n   - Clear, direct explanation\n   - One main concept at a time\n   - Define every term\n\n3. **Concrete example** (1-2 minutes)\n   - Real, specific example\n   - Walk through step by step\n\n4. **Second example** (1-2 minutes)\n   - Different context\n   - Shows the concept generalizes\n\n5. **Edge case or common mistake** (1 minute)\n   - \"A common misconception is...\"\n   - \"This breaks down when...\"\n\n6. **Summary statement** (30 seconds)\n   - Crystallize the key insight\n\n### Do Not\n\n- Rush through to cover more material\n- Assume understanding from silence\n- Use jargon without defining it\n- Give one example and move on\n- Accept \"I think I get it\" as mastery\n\n## Consolidation Between Chunks\n\nAfter mastery is demonstrated, **connect the chunk to the bigger picture**:\n\n```\nTeacher: \"Good. Let''s consolidate. You now understand:\n- Embeddings convert text to vectors (Chunk 1)\n- Similar meanings cluster together (Chunk 2)\n- LanceDB stores and searches these vectors (Chunk 3)\n\nNotice how each piece enables the next—without embeddings,\nthere''s nothing to store; without the clustering property,\nsearching would be useless.\n\nNext chunk will cover the indexing pipeline. You''ll need to\nhold all three concepts together. Ready?\"\n```\n\n## Synthesis Test (End of Session)\n\nAfter all chunks, test **integrated understanding**:\n\n### Synthesis Question Types\n\n1. **Cross-chunk integration:**\n   \"Walk me through what happens from when a document enters the system\n   to when it''s returned in a search result. Touch on all the components\n   we covered.\"\n\n2. **Novel problem:**\n   \"A user reports that searches for ''authentication'' miss documents\n   about ''login security.'' Using what you learned, diagnose the issue\n   and propose a fix.\"\n\n3. **Design defense:**\n   \"Someone proposes storing all data in just LanceDB without SQLite.\n   Argue both for and against this change.\"\n\n4. **Teaching it:**\n   \"Explain to a junior developer why this system uses two databases\n   instead of one. Keep it under 2 minutes.\"\n\n### Synthesis Threshold\nMust demonstrate integrated understanding. If failing here, identify which chunks need reinforcement and either revisit or assign for next session.\n\n## Session Management\n\n### Natural Breaks\n- After completing a major section (2-3 chunks)\n- After difficult backfill sequences\n- After 30-40 minutes of intensive learning\n- When learner shows fatigue signals\n\n### At Breaks (Provide Mastery Status)\n\n```\nGood stopping point.\n\nMASTERY STATUS:\n✓ Vector embeddings (5/5 mastery ladder, solid)\n✓ Similarity search (4/5, one edge case to review)\n⚠ LanceDB schema (3/5, passed threshold but recommend practice)\n\nCOVERED: How embeddings enable semantic search\nNEXT: Indexing pipeline, hybrid retrieval strategies\n\nContinue, or save progress for later?\n```\n\n### Resuming Sessions\n\nWhen user chooses \"Resume\" from the initialization prompt:\n\n1. **Read progress.md** to understand current state\n2. **Show status summary:**\n   ```\n   Welcome back. Here''s where we are:\n\n   MASTERED:\n   ✓ Dual storage architecture (4/4)\n   ✓ SQLite FTS5 (3.5/4)\n\n   IN PROGRESS:\n   ⚠ Vector embeddings (2/4 last attempt - needs reteach)\n\n   REMAINING:\n   ○ Indexing pipeline\n   ○ Retrieval strategies\n   ```\n3. **Run recall quiz** (3-4 questions on mastered chunks)\n4. If rusty (< 60% correct): Brief refresher, update notes in progress.md\n5. If solid (80%+ correct): Proceed with confidence\n6. **Resume at current chunk** or reteach if previous attempt failed\n7. Always reconnect: \"Last time we established X. Today we''ll build on that...\"\n\n## Tone\n\n**Baseline:** Rigorous professor—high standards, clear expectations, structured\n**Layer in:** Supportive mentor—encouraging, patient, believes in learner\n**Adapt to:** Learner''s pace, but never lower standards\n\n| Situation | Say | Avoid |\n|-----------|-----|-------|\n| Wrong answer | \"Not quite. Let''s think through this—what did we say about...\" | \"Wrong.\" / \"That''s incorrect.\" |\n| Repeated struggles | \"This is genuinely difficult material. Let''s approach it differently.\" | \"It''s easy, you should get this.\" |\n| Mastery achieved | \"Solid. You''ve demonstrated understanding.\" | \"Great job!\" / excessive praise |\n| Frustration | \"Take a breath. This confusion is normal—it means you''re learning.\" | Rushing past the difficulty |\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Mastery before advancement** — Never proceed until 80%+ demonstrated\n2. **Multiple verification levels** — Test understand, apply, AND analyze\n3. **Deep foundations** — Backfill thoroughly, never patch over gaps\n4. **Progressive complexity** — Build from novice toward expert cognition\n5. **Integrated understanding** — Connect chunks, test synthesis\n6. **High standards, high support** — Rigorous but patient\n7. **No false confidence** — \"Got it?\" tells you nothing; test instead\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:10:33.085Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Educational Agents needing advanced lesson planning and technical document transformation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级课程规划和技术文档转换功能的教育代理","ja":"教育エージェントが高度なレッスン計画と技術文書の変換機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"교육 에이전트가 고급 수업 계획과 기술 문서 변환 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Educativos que necesitan una planificación de lecciones avanzada y capacidades de transformación de documentos técnicos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents Éducatifs ayant besoin d''une planification de leçons avancée et de capacités de transformation de documents techniques.","de":"Perfekt für Bildungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Lektionsplanung und technische Dokumenten-Transformationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Educacionais que precisam de planejamento de lições avançado e capacidades de transformação de documentos técnicos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для образовательных агентов, которым необходимы расширенные возможности планирования уроков и преобразования технических документов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التعليميين الذين يحتاجون إلى تخطيط دروس متقدم وقدرات تحويل الوثائق الفنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform technical documents into rigorous learning journeys using mastery learning principles, demonstrated mastery requirements, and verification examples, leveraging references like mastery-learning-research.md and learning-science.md.","zh":"赋予代理人使用掌握学习原则、展示掌握要求和验证示例等方法，将技术文档转换为严谨的学习旅程，借鉴了 mastery-learning-research.md 和 learning-science.md 等参考资料","ja":"エージェントが技術文書を厳密な学習の旅に変換できるようにし、達成基準の原則、実証された達成要件、検証例などを使用し、mastery-learning-research.md や learning-science.md などの参考資料を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 기술 문서를 엄격한 학습 여정으로 변환할 수 있도록 하며, 마스터링 학습 원칙, 입증된 마스터링 요구 사항 및 검증 예제를 사용하고, mastery-learning-research.md 및 learning-science.md와 같은 참조 자료를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar documentos técnicos en rigurosos viajes de aprendizaje utilizando principios de aprendizaje de maestría, requisitos de maestría demostrada y ejemplos de verificación, aprovechando referencias como mastery-learning-research.md y learning-science.md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des documents techniques en parcours d''apprentissage rigoureux en utilisant des principes d''apprentissage de maîtrise, des exigences de maîtrise démontrée et des exemples de vérification, en exploitant des références telles que mastery-learning-research.md et learning-science.md.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, technische Dokumente in strenge Lernreisen zu verwandeln, indem sie Prinzipien des Meisterlernens, nachgewiesene Meisteranforderungen und Verifizierungsbeispiele nutzen, unter Ausnutzung von Referenzen wie mastery-learning-research.md und learning-science.md.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar documentos técnicos em jornadas de aprendizado rigorosas usando princípios de aprendizado de mestria, requisitos de demonstração de mestria e exemplos de verificação, aproveitando referências como mastery-learning-research.md e learning-science.md.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать технические документы в строгие образовательные пути, используя принципы освоения знаний, требования демонстрации освоения и примеры верификации, опираясь на ссылки как mastery-learning-research.md и learning-science.md.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تحويل الوثائق الفنية إلى رحلات تعليمية صارمة باستخدام مبادئ التعلم بالتجارب، ومتطلبات إثبات الإتقان وأمثلة التحقق، واستخدام المراجع مثل mastery-learning-research.md و learning-science.md."},"useCases":{"en":["Transforming technical documents into interactive learning sessions","Creating demonstrated mastery requirements for each learning stage","Generating verification examples for assessment and feedback"],"zh":["将技术文档转换为交互式学习课程","为每个学习阶段创建展示掌握要求","为评估和反馈生成验证示例"],"ja":["技術文書をインタラクティブな学習セッションに変換する","各学習段階の実証された達成要件を作成する","評価とフィードバックのための検証例を生成する"],"ko":["기술 문서를 상호작용형 학습 세션으로 변환","각 학습 단계의 검증된 마스터링 요구 사항을 생성","평가 및 피드백을 위한 검증 예제를 생성"],"es":["Transformar documentos técnicos en sesiones de aprendizaje interactivas","Crear requisitos de maestría demostrada para cada etapa de aprendizaje","Generar ejemplos de verificación para evaluación y comentarios"],"fr":["Transformer des documents techniques en sessions d''apprentissage interactives","Créer des exigences de maîtrise démontrée pour chaque étape d''apprentissage","Générer des exemples de vérification pour évaluation et rétroaction"],"de":["Technische Dokumente in interaktive Lernsitzungen umwandeln","Nachgewiesene Meisteranforderungen für jede Lernphase erstellen","Verifizierungsbeispiele für Bewertung und Feedback generieren"],"pt":["Transformar documentos técnicos em sessões de aprendizado interativo","Criar requisitos de demonstração de mestria para cada estágio de aprendizado","Gerar exemplos de verificação para avaliação e feedback"],"ru":["Преобразование технических документов в интерактивные учебные сессии","Создание требований к демонстрации освоения для каждого этапа обучения","Генерация примеров верификации для оценки и обратной связи"],"ar":["تحويل الوثائق الفنية إلى جلسات تعلم تفاعلية","إنشاء متطلبات إثبات الإتقان لكل مرحلة من مراحل التعلم","توليد أمثلة للتحقق للتقييم والتعليقات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to technical documents and learning materials","Offline and security-first deployment only","Deep understanding of learning science and mastery learning principles necessary"],"zh":["需要访问技术文档和学习材料","仅支持离线和安全优先部署","需要对学习科学和掌握学习原则有深入的理解"],"ja":["技術文書と学習資料へのアクセスが必要","オフラインとセキュリティ優先のデプロイのみをサポート","学習科学と達成基準の原則に対する深い理解が必要"],"ko":["기술 문서 및 학습 자료에 대한 액세스가 필요","오프라인 및 보안 우선 배포만 지원","학습 과학과 마스터링 학습 원칙에 대한 깊은 이해가 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso a documentos técnicos y materiales de aprendizaje","Despliegue solo en modo de seguridad y sin conexión","Conocimiento profundo de la ciencia del aprendizaje y los principios de aprendizaje de maestría necesario"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des documents techniques et à des matériaux d''apprentissage","Déploiement en mode sécurité et hors ligne uniquement","Connaissance approfondie de la science de l''apprentissage et des principes d''apprentissage de maîtrise nécessaire"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf technische Dokumente und Lernmaterialien","Bereitstellung nur im Offline- und Sicherheitsmodus","Tiefes Verständnis der Lernwissenschaft und der Meisterlernprinzipien erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso a documentos técnicos e materiais de aprendizado","Implantação offline e com prioridade à segurança","Entendimento profundo da ciência do aprendizado e princípios de aprendizado de mestria necessário"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к техническим документам и учебным материалам","Развертывание офлайн и с приоритетом безопасности","Глубокое понимание науки обучения и принципов освоения знаний необходимо"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الوثائق الفنية ومواد التعلم","التحديث دون اتصال وأولوية الأمان","فهم عميق للعلم التعلم ومبادئ التعلم بالتجارب ضروري"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"faa36cbc7bc24db027707c0fb4c930aa49b3377d5b4ec4b7c5a126553620719b","qualityScore":37}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('EvanBacon/apple-health/expo-modules', 'community', 'EvanBacon', 'apple-health', 'EvanBacon/apple-health', 'expo-modules', 0, 0, 37, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.910Z', '2026-03-02T02:20:57.018Z', '778c219951b45d3f454b9fe5f2e255380db39a3fa47dc1cd0e1aa7cbf6ef8d62', '{"id":"EvanBacon/apple-health/expo-modules","name":"expo-modules","description":{"zh":"expo-modules 为 Expo 应用程序提供了 Apple HealthKit 绑定","ja":"expo-modules は Expo アプリケーションに Apple HealthKit バインディングを提供","ko":"expo-modules는 Expo 애플리케이션에 Apple HealthKit 바인딩을 제공","es":"Bindings de Apple HealthKit para Expo. Conecta tu app con Apple HealthKit","fr":"Bindings d''Apple HealthKit pour Expo. Connectez votre app avec Apple HealthKit","de":"Bindings von Apple HealthKit für Expo. Verbinden Sie Ihre App mit Apple HealthKit","pt":"Expo-Modules é uma ligação do Apple HealthKit para Expo, permitindo aos desenvolvedores criar aplicativos de saúde","ru":"Expo-Modules - это связь с Apple HealthKit для Expo, позволяющая разработчикам создавать приложения для здоровья","ar":"expo-modules هو ربط ل Apple HealthKit من أجل Expo، مما يسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تطبيقات الصحة","en":"Apple HealthKit bindings for Expo"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"expo-modules - Apple HealthKit 绑定","ja":"expo-modules - Apple HealthKit バインディング","ko":"expo-modules - Apple HealthKit 바인딩","es":"Apple HealthKit para Expo - expo-modules","fr":"Apple HealthKit pour Expo - expo-modules","de":"Apple HealthKit für Expo - expo-modules","pt":"Ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial: Expo-Modules","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Expo-Modules для Apple HealthKit","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: expo-modules","en":"expo-modules"},"description":{"zh":"expo-modules 为 Expo 应用程序提供了 Apple HealthKit 绑定","ja":"expo-modules は Expo アプリケーションに Apple HealthKit バインディングを提供","ko":"expo-modules는 Expo 애플리케이션에 Apple HealthKit 바인딩을 제공","es":"Bindings de Apple HealthKit para Expo. Conecta tu app con Apple HealthKit","fr":"Bindings d''Apple HealthKit pour Expo. Connectez votre app avec Apple HealthKit","de":"Bindings von Apple HealthKit für Expo. Verbinden Sie Ihre App mit Apple HealthKit","pt":"Expo-Modules é uma ligação do Apple HealthKit para Expo, permitindo aos desenvolvedores criar aplicativos de saúde","ru":"Expo-Modules - это связь с Apple HealthKit для Expo, позволяющая разработчикам создавать приложения для здоровья","ar":"expo-modules هو ربط ل Apple HealthKit من أجل Expo، مما يسمح للمطورين بإنشاء تطبيقات الصحة","en":"Apple HealthKit bindings for Expo"},"definition":{"en":"Apple HealthKit bindings for Expo"},"features":{"zh":["Apple HealthKit 绑定","支持 Expo 应用程序","使用简单"],"ja":["Apple HealthKit バインディング","Expo アプリケーション対応","使用簡単"],"ko":["Apple HealthKit 바인딩","Expo 애플리케이션 지원","사용 편리"],"es":["Bindings de Apple HealthKit para Expo","Conecta tu app con Apple HealthKit","Accede a datos de salud y fitness","Integra con otros servicios de salud y fitness"],"fr":["Bindings d''Apple HealthKit pour Expo","Connectez votre app avec Apple HealthKit","Accédez à des données de santé et de fitness","Intégrez avec d''autres services de santé et de fitness"],"de":["Bindings von Apple HealthKit für Expo","Verbinden Sie Ihre App mit Apple HealthKit","Zugriff auf Gesundheits- und Fitnessdaten","Integrieren mit anderen Gesundheits- und Fitnessdiensten"],"pt":["Integração com Apple HealthKit","Criação de aplicativos de saúde","Suporte a desenvolvedores","Fácil implementação","Compatibilidade com Expo"],"ru":["Интеграция с Apple HealthKit","Создание приложений для здоровья","Поддержка разработчиков","Легкая реализация","Совместимость с Expo"],"ar":["التكامل مع Apple HealthKit","إنشاء تطبيقات الصحة","دعم المطورين","تنفيذ سهل","التوافق مع Expo"]},"keywords":{"zh":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Expo 应用程序","绑定","使用方法","安装指南"],"ja":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Expo アプリケーション","バインディング","使用方法","インストールガイド"],"ko":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Expo 애플리케이션","바인딩","사용 방법","설치 가이드"],"es":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Bindings de Apple HealthKit","Conectar con Apple HealthKit","Acceder a datos de salud y fitness","Integrar con otros servicios de salud y fitness"],"fr":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Bindings d''Apple HealthKit","Connecter avec Apple HealthKit","Accéder à des données de santé et de fitness","Intégrer avec d''autres services de santé et de fitness"],"de":["expo-modules","Apple HealthKit","Bindings von Apple HealthKit","Verbinden mit Apple HealthKit","Zugriff auf Gesundheits- und Fitnessdaten","Integrieren mit anderen Gesundheits- und Fitnessdiensten"],"pt":["como usar expo-modules","o que é expo-modules","expo-modules vs react-native","instalar expo-modules","guia de configuração do expo-modules","desenvolvedores de aplicativos de saúde","ferramentas de inteligência artificial para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать expo-modules","что такое expo-modules","expo-modules vs react-native","установить expo-modules","руководство по настройке expo-modules","разработчики приложений для здоровья","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام expo-modules","ما هو expo-modules","expo-modules vs react-native","تثبيت expo-modules","دليل إعداد expo-modules","مطورو تطبيقات الصحة","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"EvanBacon","repo":"apple-health","repoPath":"EvanBacon/apple-health","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.910Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"expo-modules","description":"Building great Expo native modules for iOS and Android. Views, APIs, Marshalling, Shared Objects, Expo Documentation, Verifying Expo modules.","bodyPreview":"## Great module standards\n\n- Design native APIs as if you contributing W3C specs for the browser, take inspiration from modern web modules. eg `std:kv-storage`, `clipboard`.\n- Aim for 100% backwards compatibility like the web.\n- Create escape hatches for single-platform functionality.\n- Avoid extraneous abstractions. Directly expose native functionality.\n- Avoid unnecessary async methods. Use sync methods when possible.\n- Prefer string union types for API options instead of boolean flags, enums,","body":"## Great module standards\n\n- Design native APIs as if you contributing W3C specs for the browser, take inspiration from modern web modules. eg `std:kv-storage`, `clipboard`.\n- Aim for 100% backwards compatibility like the web.\n- Create escape hatches for single-platform functionality.\n- Avoid extraneous abstractions. Directly expose native functionality.\n- Avoid unnecessary async methods. Use sync methods when possible.\n- Prefer string union types for API options instead of boolean flags, enums, or multiple parameters. eg instead of `capture(options: { isHighQuality: boolean })`, use `capture(options: { quality: ''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'' })`.\n- Marshalling is awesome for platform-specific APIs.\n- New Architecture only. NEVER support legacy React Native architecture.\n- ALWAYS use only Expo modules API.\n- Prefer Swift and Kotlin.\n- Use optionality for availability checks as opposed to extraneous `isAvailable` functions or constants. eg `snapshot.capture?.()` instead of `snapshot.isAvailable && snapshot.capture()`.\n- ALWAYS support the latest and greatest API features.\n\nExample of a GREAT Expo module:\n\n```ts\nimport { NativeModule } from \"expo\";\n\ndeclare class AppClipModule extends NativeModule<{}> {\n  prompt(): void;\n  isAppClip?: boolean;\n}\n\n// This call loads the native module object from the JSI.\nconst AppClipNative =\n  typeof expo !== \"undefined\"\n    ? (expo.modules.AppClip as AppClipModule) ?? {}\n    : {};\n\nif (AppClipNative?.isAppClip) {\n  navigator.appClip = {\n    prompt: AppClipNative.prompt,\n  };\n}\n\n// Add types for the global `navigator.appClip` object.\ndeclare global {\n  interface Navigator {\n    /**\n     * Only available in an App Clip context.\n     * @expo\n     */\n    appClip?: {\n      /** Open the SKOverlay */\n      prompt: () => void;\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nexport {};\n```\n\n- Simple web-style interface.\n- Global type augmentation for easy access.\n- Docs in the type definitions.\n- Optional availability checks instead of extraneous `isAvailable` methods.\n\nExample of a POOR Expo module:\n\n```ts\nimport { NativeModulesProxy } from \"expo-modules-core\";\nconst { ExpoAppClip } = NativeModulesProxy;\nexport default {\n  promptAppClip() {\n    return ExpoAppClip.promptAppClip();\n  },\n  isAppClipAvailable() {\n    return ExpoAppClip.isAppClipAvailable();\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Great documentation\n\n- If you have a function like `isAvailable()`, explain why it exists in the docs. Research cases where it may return false such as in a simulator or particular OS version.\n- Document OS version availability for functions and constants in the type definitions.\n\n## BAD module standards\n\n- APIs that are hard to import, e.g. `import * as MediaLibrary from ''expo-media-library'';` instead of `import { MediaLibrary } from ''expo/media'';`\n- Extraneous abstractions over native functionality. The native module is installing on the global, do not wrap it in another layer for no reason.\n- Extraneous async methods when sync methods are possible.\n- Boolean flags instead of string union types for options.\n- Supporting legacy React Native architecture.\n\n## Views\n\nTake API inspiration from great web component libraries like BaseUI and Radix.\n\n- https://base-ui.com/react/components/progress\n- https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives/docs/components/progress\n\nConsider if you''re building a control or a display component. Controls should have more interactive APIs, while display components should be more declarative.\n\nPrefer functions on views instead of `useImperativeHandle` + `findNodeHandle`.\n\n```swift\nAsyncFunction(\"capture\") { (view, options: Options) -> Ref in\n  return try capture(self.appContext, view)\n}\n```\n\nRemember to export views in the module:\n\n```swift\nimport ExpoModulesCore\n\npublic class ExpoWebViewModule: Module {\n  public func definition() -> ModuleDefinition {\n    Name(\"ExpoWebView\")\n\n    View(ExpoWebView.self) {}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Marshalling-style API\n\nConsider this example https://github.com/EvanBacon/expo-shared-objects-haptics-example/blob/be90e92f8dba9b0807009502ab25c423c57e640d/modules/my-module/ios/MyModule.swift#L1C1-L178C2\n\nUsing `@retroactive Convertible` and `AnyArgument` to convert between Swift types and dictionaries enables passing complex data structures across the boundary without writing custom serialization code for each type.\n\n```swift\nextension CHHapticEventParameter: @retroactive Convertible, AnyArgument {\n    public static func convert(from value: Any?, appContext: AppContext) throws -> Self {\n        guard let dict = value as? [String: Any],\n              let parameterIDRaw = dict[\"parameterID\"] as? String,\n              let value = dict[\"value\"] as? Double else {\n            throw NotADictionaryException()\n        }\n        return Self(parameterID: CHHapticEvent.ParameterID(rawValue: parameterIDRaw), value: Float(value))\n    }\n}\n\nextension CHHapticEvent: @retroactive Convertible, AnyArgument {\n    public static func convert(from value: Any?, appContext: AppContext) throws -> Self {\n        guard let dict = value as? [String: Any],\n              let eventTypeRaw = dict[\"eventType\"] as? String,\n              let relativeTime = dict[\"relativeTime\"] as? Double else {\n            throw NotADictionaryException()\n        }\n        let eventType = CHHapticEvent.EventType(rawValue: eventTypeRaw)\n        let parameters = (dict[\"parameters\"] as? [[String: Any]])?.compactMap { paramDict -> CHHapticEventParameter? in\n            try? CHHapticEventParameter.convert(from: paramDict, appContext: appContext)\n        } ?? []\n        return Self(eventType: eventType, parameters: parameters, relativeTime: relativeTime)\n    }\n}\n\nextension CHHapticDynamicParameter: @retroactive Convertible, AnyArgument {\n    public static func convert(from value: Any?, appContext: AppContext) throws -> Self {\n        guard let dict = value as? [String: Any],\n              let parameterIDRaw = dict[\"parameterID\"] as? String,\n              let value = dict[\"value\"] as? Double,\n              let relativeTime = dict[\"relativeTime\"] as? Double else {\n            throw NotADictionaryException()\n        }\n\n        return Self(parameterID: CHHapticDynamicParameter.ID(rawValue: parameterIDRaw), value: Float(value), relativeTime: relativeTime)\n    }\n}\n\nextension CHHapticPattern: @retroactive Convertible, AnyArgument {\n    public static func convert(from value: Any?, appContext: AppContext) throws -> Self {\n        guard let dict = value as? [String: Any],\n              let eventsArray = dict[\"events\"] as? [[String: Any]] else {\n            throw NotADictionaryException()\n        }\n        let events = try eventsArray.map { eventDict -> CHHapticEvent in\n            try CHHapticEvent.convert(from: eventDict, appContext: appContext)\n        }\n        let parameters = (dict[\"parameters\"] as? [[String: Any]])?.compactMap { paramDict -> CHHapticDynamicParameter? in\n            return try? CHHapticDynamicParameter.convert(from: paramDict, appContext: appContext)\n        } ?? []\n        return try Self(events: events, parameters: parameters)\n    }\n}\n\ninternal final class NotAnArrayException: Exception {\n    override var reason: String {\n        \"Given value is not an array\"\n    }\n}\n\ninternal final class IncorrectArraySizeException: GenericException<(expected: Int, actual: Int)> {\n    override var reason: String {\n        \"Given array has unexpected number of elements: \\(param.actual), expected: \\(param.expected)\"\n    }\n}\n\ninternal final class NotADictionaryException: Exception {\n    override var reason: String {\n        \"Given value is not a dictionary\"\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nLater this can be used to implement methods that accept complex data structures as arguments.\n\n```swift\nFunction(\"playPattern\") { (pattern: CHHapticPattern) in\n    let player = try hapticEngine.makePlayer(with: pattern)\n    try player.start(atTime: 0)\n}\n```\n\nUse shorthand where possible, especially when the JS value matches the Swift value:\n\n```swift\nProperty(\"__typename\") { $0.__typename }\n```\n\n## Shared objects\n\nShared objects are long-lived native instances that are shared to JS. They can be used to keep heavy state objects, such as a decoded bitmap, alive across React components, rather than spinning up a new native instance every time a component mounts.\n\n- https://docs.expo.dev/modules/shared-objects/\n- https://expo.dev/blog/the-real-world-impact-of-shared-objects\n\n## Interacting with AppDelegate\n\nTo interact with HealthKit, the module may need to respond to app lifecycle events. This can be done by implementing the `ExpoAppDelegateSubscriber` protocol.\n\n```swift\nimport ExpoModulesCore\n\npublic class ExpoHeadAppDelegateSubscriber: ExpoAppDelegateSubscriber {\n\n// Any AppDelegate methods you want to implement\n  public func application(\n    _ application: UIApplication,\n    continue userActivity: NSUserActivity,\n    restorationHandler: @escaping ([UIUserActivityRestoring]?) -> Void\n  ) -> Bool {\n    launchedActivity = userActivity\n\n   // ...\n\n    return false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThen add the subscriber to the `expo-module.config.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"platforms\": [\"apple\", \"android\", \"web\"],\n  \"apple\": {\n    \"modules\": [\"ExpoHeadModule\", ...],\n    \"appDelegateSubscribers\": [\"ExpoHeadAppDelegateSubscriber\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Expo ecosystem integration\n\n- Create a Config Plugin for setting up all permissions and entitlements.\n- Permissions APIs should follow Expo''s permission model and implement hooks.\n  - Ref: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/843d5e108ff70539ac353721d3a7765a5d08d502/packages/expo-media-library/src/MediaLibrary.ts#L502-L519\n- Document when things don''t work in Expo Go and link to dev client instructions.\n- Consider creating Expo devtools plugins for interacting with native APIs. Optimize for Claude Code usage, e.g. a Bun CLI before a UI.\n  - Ref: https://docs.expo.dev/debugging/devtools-plugins\n- If any feature launches the app or could benefit from deep linking, add an Expo Router integration. A good example is `expo-quick-actions` which has a `expo-quick-actions/router` import for automatic deep linking. Other good examples are Expo notifications (open settings, redirect notifications), widgets, siri shortcuts.\n  - Ref: https://github.com/EvanBacon/expo-quick-actions\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run `yarn expo run:ios --no-bundler` in an Expo app to headlessly compile the module and verify there are no compilation errors.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:20:57.018Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Mobile Agents requiring seamless integration with Apple HealthKit and native APIs.","zh":"适用于需要与 Apple HealthKit 和原生 API 无缝集成的移动代理。","ja":"Apple HealthKit とネイティブ API とのシームレスな統合を必要とするモバイル エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Apple HealthKit 및 네이티브 API와의無縫な통합을 필요로하는 모바일 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes móviles que requieren una integración perfecta con Apple HealthKit y APIs nativas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents mobiles nécessitant une intégration transparente avec Apple HealthKit et les API natives.","de":"Ideal für Mobile Agents, die eine nahtlose Integration mit Apple HealthKit und nativen APIs erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Móveis que exigem integração perfeita com o Apple HealthKit e APIs nativas.","ru":"Идеально для мобильных агентов, требующих бесшовной интеграции с Apple HealthKit и родными API.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النقالين الذين يتطلبون التكامل السلس مع Apple HealthKit وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات الأصلية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage Apple HealthKit bindings for Expo, utilizing standards like W3C specs and modern web modules such as std:kv-storage and clipboard, while ensuring 100% backwards compatibility and direct exposure to native functionality.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Expo 的 Apple HealthKit 绑定，利用 W3C 规范和现代 Web 模块（如 std:kv-storage 和 clipboard），同时确保 100% 向后兼容性和直接暴露于原生功能。","ja":"エージェントが Expo の Apple HealthKit バインディングを利用できるようにし、W3C 規格や std:kv-storage や clipboard などのモダンな Web モジュールを使用しながら、100% の下位互換性とネイティブ機能への直接公開を保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 Expo의 Apple HealthKit 바인딩을 사용할 수 있도록하여 W3C 규격 및 std:kv-storage 및 clipboard와 같은 현대적인 Web 모듈을 사용하면서 100% 하위 호환성을 보장하고 네이티브 기능에 직접 노출되도록합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar los enlaces de Apple HealthKit para Expo, utilizando estándares como las especificaciones W3C y módulos web modernos como std:kv-storage y clipboard, al mismo tiempo que garantiza la compatibilidad hacia atrás al 100% y la exposición directa a la funcionalidad nativa.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter les liens Apple HealthKit pour Expo, en utilisant des normes comme les spécifications W3C et des modules web modernes tels que std:kv-storage et clipboard, tout en garantissant une compatibilité ascendante à 100% et une exposition directe à la fonctionnalité native.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Apple HealthKit-Bindings für Expo zu nutzen, indem es Standards wie W3C-Spezifikationen und moderne Webmodule wie std:kv-storage und clipboard verwendet, während es gleichzeitig eine 100%ige Abwärtskompatibilität und eine direkte Exposition gegenüber der nativen Funktionalität gewährleistet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar os conjuntos de ligação do Apple HealthKit para o Expo, utilizando padrões como as especificações do W3C e módulos web modernos, como std:kv-storage e clipboard, garantindo 100% de compatibilidade para trás e exposição direta à funcionalidade nativa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать привязки Apple HealthKit для Expo, используя стандарты, такие как спецификации W3C и современные веб-модули, такие как std:kv-storage и clipboard, обеспечивая 100% обратную совместимость и прямой доступ к родной функциональности.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على الاستفادة من ربط Apple HealthKit مع Expo، باستخدام المعايير مثل مواصفات W3C ووحدات الويب الحديثة مثل std:kv-storage وclipboard، مع ضمان 100٪ من التوافق الخلفي والوصول المباشر إلى الوظائف الأصلية."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing HealthKit data synchronization","Creating native APIs with escape hatches for single-platform functionality","Developing modules with string union types for API options"],"zh":["实现 HealthKit 数据同步","使用单平台功能的逃生舱创建原生 API","开发具有字符串联合类型的模块用于 API 选项"],"ja":["HealthKit データ同期の実装","単一プラットフォーム機能のためのエスケープハッチを使用したネイティブ API の作成","API オプション用の文字列ユニオン型を使用したモジュールの開発"],"ko":["HealthKit 데이터 동기화 구현","단일 플랫폼 기능을 위한 탈출구를 사용한 네이티브 API 생성","API 옵션을 위한 문자열 유니온 타입을 사용한 모듈 개발"],"es":["Implementar la sincronización de datos de HealthKit","Crear APIs nativas con escapes para funcionalidad de una sola plataforma","Desarrollar módulos con tipos de unión de cadena para opciones de API"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre la synchronisation des données HealthKit","Créer des API natives avec des échappatoires pour la fonctionnalité d''une seule plateforme","Développer des modules avec des types d''union de chaîne pour les options d''API"],"de":["Implementierung der HealthKit-Datensynchronisation","Erstellung von nativen APIs mit Ausnahmen für Single-Platform-Funktionalität","Entwicklung von Modulen mit Zeichenfolgenvereinigungstypen für API-Optionen"],"pt":["Implementação da sincronização de dados do HealthKit","Criação de APIs nativas com escapes para funcionalidade de plataforma única","Desenvolvimento de módulos com tipos de união de string para opções de API"],"ru":["Реализация синхронизации данных HealthKit","Создание родных API с возможностью выхода для функциональности одной платформы","Разработка модулей с объединенными типами строк для опций API"],"ar":["تنفيذ مزامنة بيانات HealthKit","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الأصلية مع ملاجئ لتوظيف منصة واحدة","تطوير الوحدات ذات أنواع اتحاد السلاسل لنخبة خيارات API"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Expo environment","Apple HealthKit compatibility needed","Native functionality limitations apply"],"zh":["需要 Expo 环境","需要 Apple HealthKit 兼容性","原生功能限制适用"],"ja":["Expo 環境が必要","Apple HealthKit との互換性が必要","ネイティブ機能の制限が適用される"],"ko":["Expo 환경 필요","Apple HealthKit 호환성 필요","네이티브 기능 제한 사항 적용"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Expo","Se requiere compatibilidad con Apple HealthKit","Se aplican limitaciones de funcionalidad nativa"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Expo","La compatibilité avec Apple HealthKit est requise","Les limitations de fonctionnalité native s''appliquent"],"de":["Benötigt Expo-Umgebung","Apple HealthKit-Kompatibilität erforderlich","Einschränkungen der nativen Funktionalität gelten"],"pt":["Exige ambiente Expo","Compatibilidade com o Apple HealthKit necessária","Limitações de funcionalidade nativa se aplicam"],"ru":["Требует среды Expo","Необходимо совместимость с Apple HealthKit","Применяются ограничения родной функциональности"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Expo","يتطلب توافق مع Apple HealthKit","تطبق قيود الوظائف الأصلية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"778c219951b45d3f454b9fe5f2e255380db39a3fa47dc1cd0e1aa7cbf6ef8d62","qualityScore":37}');
