:"github-dev"},"description":{"zh":"GitHub Dev提供Autonomous AI agent模板，用于开发和GTM自动化，帮助开发者提高效率","ja":"GitHub Devは、開発とGTM自動化用のAutonomous AIエージェントテンプレートを提供し、開発者の効率を向上させる","ko":"깃허브 Dev는 개발과 GTM 자동화를 위한 자율형 AI 에이전트 템플릿을 제공하여 개발자의 효율성을 향상시킵니다","es":"Las plantillas de agentes de IA para desarrollo y automatización de github-dev mejoran la eficiencia del flujo de trabajo","fr":"Les modèles d''agents de l''IA pour le développement et l''automatisation de github-dev améliorent l''efficacité du flux de travail","de":"Die Vorlagen für KI-Agents für Entwicklung und Automatisierung von github-dev verbessern die Effizienz des Arbeitsflusses","pt":"Os modelos de agentes de IA autônomos para desenvolvimento e automação de GTM permitem uma integração perfeita","ru":"ИИ Агенты для автоматизации разработки и GTM обеспечивают идеальную интеграцию","ar":"القوالب الأوتوماتيكية لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي للتنمية وتأتمتة GTM تمكنك من التكامل المثالي","en":"Autonomous AI agent templates for development and GTM automation"},"definition":{"en":"Autonomous AI agent templates for development and GTM automation"},"features":{"zh":["预构建的Autonomous AI agent模板","支持开发和GTM自动化","提高开发效率和生产力","简化开发和GTM流程","支持多种开发语言和框架"],"ja":["事前構築済みのAutonomous AIエージェントテンプレート","開発とGTM自動化のサポート","開発効率と生産性の向上","開発とGTMプロセスの簡素化","複数の開発言語とフレームワークのサポート"],"ko":["미리 구축된 자율형 AI 에이전트 템플릿","개발과 GTM 자동화 지원","개발 효율성과 생산성 향상","개발과 GTM 프로세스 간소화","다양한 개발 언어와 프레임워크 지원"],"es":["Automatización de tareas de desarrollo","Integración con GitHub","Soporte para múltiples lenguajes de programación","CLI para ejecución de comandos","Plantillas personalizables para proyectos"],"fr":["Automatisation des tâches de développement","Intégration avec GitHub","Prise en charge de plusieurs langages de programmation","CLI pour l''exécution de commandes","Modèles personnalisables pour les projets"],"de":["Automatisierung von Entwicklungs-Aufgaben","Integration mit GitHub","Unterstützung für mehrere Programmiersprachen","CLI für die Ausführung von Befehlen","Anpassbare Vorlagen für Projekte"],"pt":["Integração com GitHub","Automação de desenvolvimento","GTM automático","Modelos de agentes de IA personalizados","Suporte a React, Python e Node.js"],"ru":["Интеграция с GitHub","Автоматизация разработки","Автоматизация GTM","Пользовательские модели ИИ Агентов","Поддержка React, Python и Node.js"],"ar":["التكامل مع GitHub","تأتمتة التنمية","تأتمتة GTM","نماذج وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المخصصة","دعم React و Python و Node.js"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitHub Dev","AI开发自动化","GTM自动化","Autonomous AI agent","开发效率","生产力","开发框架","如何使用GitHub Dev","GitHub Dev替代品"],"ja":["GitHub Dev","AIエージェント","GTM自動化","Autonomous AIエージェント","開発効率","生産性","開発フレームワーク","GitHub Devの使い方","GitHub Devの代替"],"ko":["깃허브 Dev","AI 에이전트","GTM 자동화","자율형 AI 에이전트","개발 효율성","생산성","개발 프레임워크","깃허브 Dev 사용법","깃허브 Dev 대안"],"es":["cómo usar github-dev","qué es un agente de IA","alternativas a github-dev","github-dev vs jenkins","instalación de github-dev","guía de configuración de github-dev"],"fr":["comment utiliser github-dev","qu''est-ce qu''un agent de l''IA","alternatives à github-dev","github-dev vs jenkins","installation de github-dev","guide de configuration de github-dev"],"de":["wie man github-dev verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu github-dev","github-dev vs jenkins","Installation von github-dev","Konfigurationsanleitung für github-dev"],"pt":["como usar agentes de IA","o que são agentes de IA","agentes de IA alternativos","agentes de IA vs competitors","instalar agentes de IA","guia de configuração de agentes de IA"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое ИИ Агенты","ИИ Агенты альтернативы","ИИ Агенты vs конкуренты","установить ИИ Агенты","руководство по настройке ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل المنافسين","تثبيت وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","دليل إعداد وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"consuelohq","repo":"openengineer","repoPath":"consuelohq/openengineer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:11.070Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"github-dev","description":"Remote development via GitHub API. Write code, create branches, commit files, and create PRs — all without a local clone. Pull tasks from Linear and implement them entirely through GitHub. Use when Ko wants features built remotely while working locally on other things.","bodyPreview":"# GitHub Remote Development\n\nBuild features entirely through GitHub''s API — no local clone needed. Pull tasks from Linear, create branches, write code, batch commit, create PRs, and auto-sync task status.\n\n**Why this exists:** Ko works on multiple things at once. When coming to this project, he''s already working on something locally. This skill lets the agent develop features in parallel without touching the local machine. You could have 10 sessions each working on different features simultaneou","body":"# GitHub Remote Development\n\nBuild features entirely through GitHub''s API — no local clone needed. Pull tasks from Linear, create branches, write code, batch commit, create PRs, and auto-sync task status.\n\n**Why this exists:** Ko works on multiple things at once. When coming to this project, he''s already working on something locally. This skill lets the agent develop features in parallel without touching the local machine. You could have 10 sessions each working on different features simultaneously.\n\n## Default Repo\n\n`kokayicobb/consuelo_on_call_coaching`\n\nOverride with `--repo owner/name` on any command.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- `gh` CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/gh` and authenticated\n- `LINEAR_API_KEY` set as env var (or available in `.agent/linear-api.sh`)\n- `requests` Python library (for Linear API calls)\n\n## Two Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: From Linear Task (default)\n\nKo says something like \"pull task CON-456 and implement it\" or \"work on the auth feature from Linear.\"\n\n**Steps:**\n\n1. **Fetch the task spec** — run `fetch_task.py` to pull the task from Linear and save as markdown\n2. **Read the markdown spec** — understand requirements, acceptance criteria, comments\n3. **Start the dev session** — this creates a branch and updates Linear status\n4. **Write code** — use the GitHub API to read existing files, write new files, update files\n5. **Commit** — batch commit all changes atomically\n6. **Create PR** — auto-generates body with Linear linking, moves task to \"In Review\"\n\n**Python usage (in agent context):**\n\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/Users/kokayi/Dev/claude-agent-workflow/.opencode/skills/github-dev\")\nfrom github_dev import RemoteDev\n\ndev = RemoteDev()\n\n# Start from a Linear task\nsummary = dev.start_task(\"CON-456\")\n# This: fetches task → saves spec → creates branch → updates Linear\n\n# Read the saved spec to understand what to build\n# The spec file is at: .opencode/skills/github-dev/tasks/CON-456.md\n\n# Read existing code to understand the codebase\ncontent = dev.read_file(\"src/components/Auth.tsx\")\ntree = dev.get_repo_structure(\"src/components/\")\n\n# Write new code (staged for batch commit)\ndev.write_file(\"src/components/NewFeature.tsx\", new_component_code)\ndev.write_file(\"src/utils/helper.ts\", helper_code)\ndev.write_file(\"src/tests/NewFeature.test.tsx\", test_code)\n\n# Commit all staged files atomically\ndev.commit(\"feat: implement new feature with helper utils and tests\")\n\n# Maybe write more code and commit again\ndev.write_file(\"src/styles/NewFeature.css\", css_code)\ndev.commit(\"style: add styling for new feature\")\n\n# Create PR when done (auto-links to Linear, moves task to \"In Review\")\npr = dev.create_pr()\n```\n\n**CLI usage:**\n\n```bash\n# Fetch task spec (saves to tasks/CON-456.md)\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/fetch_task.py CON-456\n\n# Start a dev session\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev task CON-456\n\n# Create a branch without a Linear task\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev create-branch \"add user auth flow\"\n\n# Read files, list directories\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev read src/file.tsx\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev ls src/components/\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev tree src/\n\n# Write/stage files for commit\necho ''file content'' | python3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev write src/new.tsx\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev write src/file.tsx --content-file /tmp/code.tsx\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev write src/quick.tsx --content \"const x = 1;\" --immediate\n\n# See what''s staged\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev staged\n\n# Commit all staged files (atomic batch via Git Trees API)\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev commit \"feat: add new component\"\n\n# Create a PR for the current branch\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev create-pr --label kiro --label enhancement\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev create-pr --title \"feat: user auth\" --label kiro\n\n# Check session status\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev status\n\n# Resume a previous session\npython3 .opencode/skills/github-dev/dev resume\n```\n\n### Workflow 2: From Existing PR\n\nKo says something like \"work on PR #789, fix the review comments\" or \"push changes to that PR.\"\n\n**Steps:**\n\n1. **Attach to the PR** — fetches PR info, sets the branch\n2. **Read the PR diff** — understand what''s already changed\n3. **Make changes** — read/write files on the PR''s branch\n4. **Commit** — push changes to the PR\n\n```python\ndev = RemoteDev()\n\n# Attach to existing PR\ndev.work_on_pr(789)\n\n# Read the current state\ncontent = dev.read_file(\"src/fix-me.tsx\")\n\n# Make changes\ndev.write_file(\"src/fix-me.tsx\", fixed_content)\ndev.commit(\"fix: address review comments\")\n```\n\n## Branch Naming Convention\n\n`remote/{repo_name}-{4char_hash}--{kebab-description}`\n\nExample: `remote/consuelo_on_call_coaching-a3f2--implement-user-auth-flow`\n\nThe `remote/` prefix distinguishes these from the `agent/` prefix used by the local agent workflow.\n\n## File Operations\n\n### Reading Files\n\n```python\n# Single file\ncontent = dev.read_file(\"src/components/Auth.tsx\")\n\n# Directory listing\nitems = dev.list_files(\"src/components/\")\n# Returns: [{\"name\": \"Auth.tsx\", \"type\": \"file\", \"size\": 1234}, ...]\n\n# Full repo tree (filtered)\nfiles = dev.get_repo_structure(\"src/\")\n# Returns: [\"src/app.tsx\", \"src/index.tsx\", ...]\n```\n\n### Writing Files (Staging)\n\nFiles are staged by default and committed as a batch:\n\n```python\n# Stage files\ndev.write_file(\"src/new.tsx\", code)\ndev.write_file(\"src/utils.ts\", utils)\n\n# Check what''s staged\ndev.staged_files()  # [\"src/new.tsx\", \"src/utils.ts\"]\n\n# Unstage a file\ndev.unstage(\"src/utils.ts\")\n\n# Commit all staged files\ndev.commit(\"feat: add new component\")\n```\n\nFor single-file immediate commits:\n\n```python\ndev.write_file(\"src/quick-fix.tsx\", code, stage=False)\n# Committed immediately\n```\n\n### Deleting Files\n\n```python\ndev.delete_file(\"src/old-file.tsx\")  # Staged\ndev.commit(\"chore: remove old file\")\n\ndev.delete_file(\"src/old-file.tsx\", stage=False)  # Immediate\n```\n\n## Batch Commits (Git Trees API)\n\nThe `commit()` method uses the Git Trees API for atomic multi-file commits. This means:\n\n- All files are committed in a single operation (no partial commits)\n- Much more efficient than one-file-at-a-time for real coding work\n- Creates proper git history (one commit per logical change)\n\n## Linear Integration\n\n### Auto-Status Sync\n\n| Event | Linear Status | Action |\n|-------|---------------|--------|\n| `start_task()` called | In Progress | Adds comment with branch name |\n| `create_pr()` called | In Review | Adds comment with PR link |\n\n### Task Spec Files\n\nFetched tasks are saved as markdown in `tasks/`:\n\n```\n.opencode/skills/github-dev/tasks/\n├── CON-456.md      # Full spec with description, criteria, comments\n├── CON-789.md\n└── .session-state.json  # Current session state for resumption\n```\n\nEach task file includes:\n- Metadata (priority, state, labels, dates)\n- Full description from Linear\n- Acceptance criteria\n- All comments (with authors and dates)\n- Subtasks (if any)\n- Attachments/links\n\n## Session Persistence\n\nThe skill saves session state to `.session-state.json` so you can resume:\n\n```python\ndev = RemoteDev()\nif dev.resume():\n    # Picks up where you left off (same branch, task, PR)\n    dev.write_file(\"src/more-code.tsx\", code)\n    dev.commit(\"feat: continue implementation\")\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n### When to Ask Ko\n\nIf Ko''s instructions are ambiguous about which workflow to use:\n\n- **\"Work on CON-456\"** → Workflow 1 (Linear task)\n- **\"Fix PR #789\"** → Workflow 2 (existing PR)\n- **\"Implement the auth feature\"** → Ask: \"should I pull from a specific Linear task or create a fresh branch?\"\n- **\"Push changes to the feature branch\"** → Ask: \"which PR or branch?\"\n\n### Rate Limits\n\nGitHub API has rate limits (5,000 requests/hour for authenticated users). Each file read/write is 1-2 API calls. Batch commits are more efficient (1 call per file for blobs + 3 fixed calls). For a typical feature (reading 10 files, writing 5), that''s ~25 API calls — well within limits.\n\n### File Size Limits\n\nThe Contents API has a 100MB limit per file. Normal source code files are well within this. If you need to handle binary files or very large files, use the Git Blobs API directly (already used in batch_commit).\n\n### Error Handling\n\n- If a branch creation fails (name conflict), the error is printed and `start_task()` raises\n- If a file write fails, the error is printed but other staged files can still be committed\n- If Linear API is unavailable, the GitHub operations still work (just no status sync)\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\ngithub-dev/\n├── SKILL.md            # This file — instructions for the agent\n├── github_api.py       # GitHub API client (gh CLI + gh api hybrid)\n├── linear_api.py       # Linear GraphQL client\n├── fetch_task.py       # CLI: pull task → markdown\n├── github_dev.py       # Main orchestrator (RemoteDev class)\n├── dev                 # Entry point script\n└── tasks/              # Saved task specs and session state\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n- **github_api.py** — All GitHub operations. Uses `gh` CLI for PRs/reviews and `gh api` for file CRUD, branches, and batch commits. No Linear awareness.\n- **linear_api.py** — All Linear operations. Fetches tasks by ID, updates status, adds comments. No GitHub awareness.\n- **fetch_task.py** — Standalone CLI script. Pulls a task and writes a markdown file. Designed to be called before the agent starts reading (saves context window).\n- **github_dev.py** — The brain. Ties GitHub + Linear together. Manages staging, session state, and the two workflows.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:27:48.010Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous Development Agents requiring parallel feature development without local environment conflicts.","zh":"非常适合需要并行功能开发且无本地环境冲突的自主开发Agent。","ja":"ローカル環境の競合なしで並行機能開発を必要とする自律開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"로컬 환경 충돌 없이 병렬 기능 개발이 필요한 자율 개발 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Autonomous Development Agents que requieren desarrollo de características en paralelo sin conflictos en el entorno local.","fr":"Parfait pour les Autonomous Development Agents nécessitant un développement de fonctionnalités en parallèle sans conflits d''environnement local.","de":"Perfekt für Autonomous Development Agents, die parallele Feature-Entwicklung ohne lokale Umweltkonflikte erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Autónomos que requerem desenvolvimento de funcionalidades em paralelo sem conflitos de ambiente local.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Автономных Агентов Разработки, требующих параллельной разработки функций без конфликтов локальной среды.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير المستقليين الذين يتطلبون تطوير ميزات متوازية دون تعارضات في البيئة المحلية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables full GitHub API-driven development workflow from task ingestion to PR creation, including branch management, batch commits, and automated status synchronization with project management tools like Linear. Eliminates local cloning requirements for true parallel development.","zh":"支持从任务接收到PR创建的全GitHub API驱动开发工作流，包括分支管理、批量提交以及与Linear等项目管理工作工具的自动化状态同步。无需本地克隆即可实现真正的并行开发。","ja":"タスクの取り込みからPR作成まで、ブランチ管理、バッチコミット、Linearなどのプロジェクト管理ツールとの自動化されたステータス同期を含む、完全なGitHub API駆動の開発ワークフローを実現します。真の並行開発のためにローカルクローンの要件を排除します。","ko":"작업 수신부터 PR 생성에 이르는 전체 GitHub API 기반 개발 워크플로우를 가능하게 하며, 여기에는 브랜치 관리, 배치 커밋 및 Linear와 같은 프로젝트 관리 도구와의 자동화된 상태 동기화가 포함됩니다. 진정한 병렬 개발을 위해 로컬 클론 요구 사항을 제거합니다.","es":"Permite un flujo de trabajo de desarrollo completo impulsado por la GitHub API, desde la ingesta de tareas hasta la creación de PR, incluyendo la gestión de ramas, commits por lotes y la sincronización automatizada de estado con herramientas de gestión de proyectos como Linear. Elimina los requisitos de clonación local para un desarrollo paralelo real.","fr":"Permet un flux de travail de développement complet piloté par la GitHub API, de l''ingestion des tâches à la création de PR, y compris la gestion des branches, les commits par lots et la synchronisation automatisée des statuts avec les outils de gestion de projet comme Linear. Élimine les besoins de clonage local pour un véritable développement parallèle.","de":"Ermöglicht einen vollständigen GitHub API-gesteuerten Entwicklungs-Workflow von der Aufgabenaufnahme bis zur PR-Erstellung, einschließlich Branch-Management, Batch-Commit und automatisierter Statussynchronisation mit Projektmanagement-Tools wie Linear. Beseitigt die Notwendigkeit des lokalen Klonens für echte parallele Entwicklung.","pt":"Permite um fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento completo orientado pela API do GitHub, desde a ingestão de tarefas até a criação de PRs, incluindo gestão de branches, commits em lote e sincronização automatizada de status com ferramentas de gestão de projetos como o Linear. Elimina a necessidade de clonagem local para um verdadeiro desenvolvimento paralelo.","ru":"Обеспечивает полный рабочий процесс разработки на основе GitHub API, от получения задач до создания PR, включая управление ветками, пакетные коммиты и автоматизированную синхронизацию статуса с инструментами управления проектами, такими как Linear. Устраняет необходимость локального клонирования для истинной параллельной разработки.","ar":"يتيح سير عمل تطوير كامل مدفوعًا بواجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub من استيعاب المهمة حتى إنشاء طلب السحب، بما في ذلك إدارة الفروع، عمليات الإيداع المجمعة، والمزامنة التلقائية للحالة مع أدوات إدارة المشاريع مثل Linear. يلغي متطلبات الاستنساخ المحلي للتطوير المتوازي الحقيقي."},"useCases":{"en":["Pulling development tasks directly from Linear","Creating feature branches via GitHub API","Writing and committing code in batch operations","Automating PR creation and task status synchronization"],"zh":["直接从Linear拉取开发任务","通过GitHub API创建功能分支","在批量操作中编写和提交代码","自动化PR创建和任务状态同步"],"ja":["Linearから開発タスクを直接プル","GitHub APIを介した機能ブランチの作成","バッチ操作でのコードの記述とコミット","PR作成とタスクステータス同期の自動化"],"ko":["Linear에서 개발 작업 직접 가져오기","GitHub API를 통한 기능 브랜치 생성","배치 작업에서 코드 작성 및 커밋","PR 생성 및 작업 상태 동기화 자동화"],"es":["Extraer tareas de desarrollo directamente desde Linear","Crear ramas de características mediante la GitHub API","Escribir y realizar commits de código en operaciones por lotes","Automatizar la creación de PR y la sincronización del estado de las tareas"],"fr":["Récupération des tâches de développement directement depuis Linear","Création de branches de fonctionnalités via la GitHub API","Écriture et commit du code dans des opérations par lots","Automatisation de la création de PR et de la synchronisation du statut des tâches"],"de":["Entwicklungsaufgaben direkt aus Linear ziehen","Erstellen von Feature-Branches über die GitHub API","Schreiben und Committen von Code in Batch-Operationen","Automatisieren der PR-Erstellung und der Aufgabenstatussynchronisation"],"pt":["Puxar tarefas de desenvolvimento diretamente do Linear","Criar branches de funcionalidades via GitHub API","Escrever e fazer commit de código em operações em lote","Automatizar a criação de PRs e a sincronização do estado das tarefas"],"ru":["Получение задач разработки непосредственно из Linear","Создание feature branches через GitHub API","Написание и коммит кода в пакетных операциях","Автоматизация создания PR и синхронизации статуса задач"],"ar":["سحب مهام التطوير مباشرة من Linear","إنشاء فروع الميزات عبر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub","كتابة التعليمات البرمجية وإيداعها في عمليات مجمعة","أتمتة إنشاء طلبات السحب ومزامنة حالة المهمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub API access","Dependent on Linear integration for task management","No local development environment access"],"zh":["需要GitHub API访问权限","任务管理依赖Linear集成","无法访问本地开发环境"],"ja":["GitHub APIへのアクセスが必要","タスク管理はLinearインテグレーションに依存","ローカル開発環境へのアクセス不可"],"ko":["GitHub API 액세스 권한 필요","작업 관리에 Linear 통합 의존","로컬 개발 환경 액세스 불가"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la GitHub API","Dependiente de la integración con Linear para la gestión de tareas","Sin acceso al entorno de desarrollo local"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la GitHub API","Dépend de l''intégration Linear pour la gestion des tâches","Pas d''accès à l''environnement de développement local"],"de":["Erfordert GitHub API-Zugriff","Abhängig von der Linear-Integration für das Aufgabenmanagement","Kein Zugriff auf die lokale Entwicklungsumgebung"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API do GitHub","Dependente da integração com Linear para gestão de tarefas","Sem acesso ao ambiente de desenvolvimento local"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к GitHub API","Зависит от интеграции с Linear для управления задачами","Нет доступа к локальной среде разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub","يعتمد على تكامل Linear لإدارة المهام","لا يوجد وصول إلى بيئة التطوير المحلية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"5f3799534ac12c4a3713c627dc87679e7d84832e4290894768c659fe10f69609","qualityScore":37}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('chrispangg/deepagentsdk/content-writer', 'community', 'chrispangg', 'deepagentsdk', 'chrispangg/deepagentsdk', 'content-writer', 0, 0, 37, '2026-03-02T01:56:11.078Z', '2026-03-02T03:29:17.209Z', '879faed0bbb5770dc73f2027b7637b607fa0a7c70d0e8f6eef03f2435dd02941', '{"id":"chrispangg/deepagentsdk/content-writer","name":"content-writer","description":{"zh":"content-writer是一个基于Vercel AI SDK v6构建的AI代理框架，帮助开发者快速集成AI功能到应用中，支持多种开发语言和平台。","ja":"content-writerは、Vercel AI SDK v6を基盤とするAIエージェントフレームワークで、開発者がアプリにAI機能を簡単に統合できるように設計されています。","ko":"content-writer는 Vercel AI SDK v6를 기반으로 한 AI 에이전트 프레임워크로, 개발자가 애플리케이션에 AI 기능을 쉽게 통합할 수 있도록 지원합니다.","es":"Content Writer es un framework de Deep Agent Harness construido con Vercel AI SDK v6 para desarrolladores","fr":"Content Writer est un framework de Deep Agent Harness construit avec Vercel AI SDK v6 pour les développeurs","de":"Content Writer ist ein Framework von Deep Agent Harness, entwickelt mit Vercel AI SDK v6 für Entwickler","pt":"O content-writer é um framework de agente de IA construído com Vercel''s AI SDK v6, projetado para automatizar e otimizar a criação de conteúdo técnico para desenvolvedores.","ru":"content-writer — это фреймворк для ИИ агентов, созданный на Vercel AI SDK v6, предназначенный для автоматизации и оптимизации создания технического контента для разработчиков.","ar":"content-writer هو إطار عمل لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مبني على Vercel AI SDK v6، مصمم لأتمتة وتحسين إنشاء المحتوى التقني للمطورين.","en":"A Deep Agent Harness framework built with Vercel''s AI SDK v6"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"使用Vercel AI SDK v6构建AI代理框架content-writer","ja":"Vercel AI SDK v6で構築されたAIエージェントフレームワーク","ko":"Vercel AI SDK v6로 구축된 AI 에이전트 프레임워크","es":"Herramientas de AI: Content Writer con Vercel AI SDK","fr":"Outils d''IA: Content Writer avec Vercel AI SDK","de":"KI-Tools: Content Writer mit Vercel AI SDK","pt":"content-writer: Ferramenta de IA para Agentes de Conteúdo...","ru":"content-writer: ИИ Агенты для создания контента на Vercel...","ar":"content-writer: أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي لوكلاء المحتوى باست...","en":"content-writer"},"description":{"zh":"content-writer是一个基于Vercel AI SDK v6构建的AI代理框架，帮助开发者快速集成AI功能到应用中，支持多种开发语言和平台。","ja":"content-writerは、Vercel AI SDK v6を基盤とするAIエージェントフレームワークで、開発者がアプリにAI機能を簡単に統合できるように設計されています。","ko":"content-writer는 Vercel AI SDK v6를 기반으로 한 AI 에이전트 프레임워크로, 개발자가 애플리케이션에 AI 기능을 쉽게 통합할 수 있도록 지원합니다.","es":"Content Writer es un framework de Deep Agent Harness construido con Vercel AI SDK v6 para desarrolladores","fr":"Content Writer est un framework de Deep Agent Harness construit avec Vercel AI SDK v6 pour les développeurs","de":"Content Writer ist ein Framework von Deep Agent Harness, entwickelt mit Vercel AI SDK v6 für Entwickler","pt":"O content-writer é um framework de agente de IA construído com Vercel''s AI SDK v6, projetado para automatizar e otimizar a criação de conteúdo técnico para d...","ru":"content-writer — это фреймворк для ИИ агентов, созданный на Vercel AI SDK v6, предназначенный для автоматизации и оптимизации создания технического контента ...","ar":"content-writer هو إطار عمل لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مبني على Vercel AI SDK v6، مصمم لأتمتة وتحسين إنشاء المحتوى التقني للمطورين.","en":"A Deep Agent Harness framework built with Vercel''s AI SDK v6"},"definition":{"en":"A Deep Agent Harness framework built with Vercel''s AI SDK v6"},"features":{"zh":["基于Vercel AI SDK v6构建","支持React和Node.js集成","提供高效的AI代理开发工具","简化AI功能部署流程","兼容多种开发环境","开源且社区支持"],"ja":["Vercel AI SDK v6ベースの構築","ReactとNode.jsの統合サポート","効率的なAIエージェント開発ツール","AI機能のデプロイプロセス簡素化","多様な開発環境との互換性","オープンソースとコミュニティサポート"],"ko":["Vercel AI SDK v6 기반 구축","React 및 Node.js 통합 지원","효율적인 AI 에이전트 개발 도구","AI 기능 배포 프로세스 간소화","다양한 개발 환경 호환성","오픈 소스 및 커뮤니티 지원"],"es":["Integración con Vercel AI SDK v6","Desarrollo de aplicaciones de AI","Herramientas de contenido avanzadas","Compatibilidad con Node.js y React","CLI para desarrollo rápido"],"fr":["Intégration avec Vercel AI SDK v6","Développement d''applications d''IA","Outils de contenu avancés","Compatibilité avec Node.js et React","CLI pour développement rapide"],"de":["Integration mit Vercel AI SDK v6","Entwicklung von KI-Anwendungen","Erweiterte Inhalts-Tools","Kompatibilität mit Node.js und React","CLI für schnelles Entwicklung"],"pt":["Construído com Vercel AI SDK v6 para integração moderna","Framework Deep Agent Harness para automação de agentes de IA","Geração de conteúdo técnico otimizado para SEO","Suporte para modelos de linguagem avançados (LLMs)","Configuração simplificada com CLI e Node.js","Documentação completa para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Построен на Vercel AI SDK v6 для современной интеграции","Фреймворк Deep Agent Harness для автоматизации ИИ агентов","Генерация технического контента с оптимизацией для SEO","Поддержка продвинутых языковых моделей (LLMs)","Упрощенная настройка с CLI и Node.js","Полная документация для разработчиков"],"ar":["مبني على Vercel AI SDK v6 للتكامل الحديث","إطار عمل Deep Agent Harness لأتمتة وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","إنشاء محتوى تقني مُحسن لمحركات البحث (SEO)","دعم نماذج اللغة المتقدمة (LLMs)","إعداد مبسط باستخدام CLI وNode.js","توثيق شامل للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI代理框架","Vercel AI SDK使用指南","content-writer安装","AI工具集成","React AI代理","Node.js AI开发","content-writer vs其他框架","如何部署AI代理"],"ja":["AIエージェントフレームワーク","Vercel AI SDK使い方","content-writerインストール","AIツール統合","React AIエージェント","Node.js AI開発","content-writer対他のフレームワーク","AIエージェントデプロイ方法"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 프레임워크","Vercel AI SDK 사용법","content-writer 설치","AI 도구 통합","React AI 에이전트","Node.js AI 개발","content-writer 대안","AI 에이전트 배포 방법"],"es":["cómo usar Content Writer","qué es un agente de IA","alternativas a Content Writer","Content Writer vs otros frameworks","instalación de Content Writer","guía de configuración de Content Writer"],"fr":["comment utiliser Content Writer","qu''est-ce qu''un agent d''IA","alternatives à Content Writer","Content Writer vs autres frameworks","installation de Content Writer","guide de configuration de Content Writer"],"de":["wie man Content Writer verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu Content Writer","Content Writer vs andere Frameworks","Installation von Content Writer","Konfigurationsanleitung für Content Writer"],"pt":["como usar content-writer","ferramentas de IA para conteúdo","Vercel AI SDK v6 tutorial","content-writer install","agentes de IA para desenvolvedores","automação de conteúdo técnico","content-writer vs outras ferramentas","Deep Agent Harness framework","setup content-writer guide","modelos de linguagem para geração de conteúdo"],"ru":["как использовать content-writer","ИИ инструменты для контента","Vercel AI SDK v6 руководство","content-writer установка","ИИ агенты для разработчиков","автоматизация технического контента","content-writer vs альтернативы","фреймворк Deep Agent Harness","настройка content-writer гайд","языковые модели для генерации контента"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام content-writer","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمحتوى","Vercel AI SDK v6 tutorial","تثبيت content-writer","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أتمتة المحتوى التقني","content-writer مقابل البدائل","إطار عمل Deep Agent Harness","دليل إعداد content-writer","نماذج اللغة لإنشاء المحتوى"]}},"owner":"chrispangg","repo":"deepagentsdk","repoPath":"chrispangg/deepagentsdk","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:11.078Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"content-writer","description":"Writing content across different platforms and styles. This skill should be used when creating blog posts, LinkedIn posts, X/Twitter threads, technical documentation, or other written content. It intelligently selects the appropriate writing style based on the platform, audience, and content type, then applies that style consistently throughout the piece.","bodyPreview":"# Content Writer\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill enables writing high-quality content across different platforms and audiences. It dynamically selects the appropriate writing style based on the task, then applies that style consistently. Available styles include deep technical blog posts, social media content (LinkedIn, X/Twitter), tutorials, and more.\n\n## Style Selection\n\nBefore writing, determine the appropriate style based on these factors:\n\n| Factor | Consider |\n|--------|----------|\n| **Platform**","body":"# Content Writer\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill enables writing high-quality content across different platforms and audiences. It dynamically selects the appropriate writing style based on the task, then applies that style consistently. Available styles include deep technical blog posts, social media content (LinkedIn, X/Twitter), tutorials, and more.\n\n## Style Selection\n\nBefore writing, determine the appropriate style based on these factors:\n\n| Factor | Consider |\n|--------|----------|\n| **Platform** | Blog, LinkedIn, X/Twitter, documentation, newsletter |\n| **Audience** | Engineers, executives, general tech audience, developers |\n| **Depth** | Deep-dive technical, lightweight explainer, announcement |\n| **Tone** | Authoritative, conversational, promotional, educational |\n| **Length** | Long-form (2000+ words), medium (500-1500), short (<500), thread |\n\n### Style Decision Tree\n\n```\nIs this for social media?\n├─ Yes → LinkedIn or X/Twitter style\n│   ├─ Professional/B2B → LinkedIn Style\n│   └─ Tech community/casual → X/Twitter Style\n│\n└─ No → Is this a technical blog post?\n    ├─ Yes → What voice/style?\n    │   ├─ Karpathy-style (conversational, personal, pragmatic) → Karpathy Style\n    │   ├─ Opinion-forward analysis → Deep Technical Style\n    │   ├─ Lightweight explainer → Simplified Technical Style\n    │   └─ Tutorial/how-to → Tutorial Style\n    │\n    └─ No → What type?\n        ├─ Announcement → Announcement Style\n        ├─ Newsletter → Newsletter Style\n        └─ Documentation → Documentation Style\n```\n\n## Available Styles\n\n### 1. Karpathy Style (Conversational Technical)\n\n**Use when:** Writing technical content that feels personal and accessible. Best for blog posts about AI/ML, tutorials, or technical essays where you want the voice of an expert friend explaining things over coffee.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- First-person, conversational tone (\"I''ve found that...\", \"Here''s what I learned...\")\n- Starts with personal experience or intriguing premise\n- Progressive complexity (simple → detailed)\n- Dry wit and occasional humor\n- Honest about limitations and failures\n- Pragmatic (\"It only has to be right more often than not\")\n- Numbered frameworks and structured approaches\n- Memorable, quotable lines\n\n**Load:** `references/karpathy-style.md` for comprehensive guidance\n\n**Core Philosophy:** \"Don''t be a hero. Start simple. Be patient.\"\n\n**Opening Hooks (choose one):**\n\n| Pattern | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Personal experience | \"I still remember when I trained my first recurrent network...\" |\n| Intriguing premise | \"We''re going to feed 2 million selfies to a neural network and have it tell us what makes a selfie good.\" |\n| Leaky abstraction | \"Neural nets are not ''off-the-shelf'' technology the second you deviate slightly from training an ImageNet classifier.\" |\n| Strong observation | \"Trees are solidified air.\" |\n\n**Example opening:**\n> \"I''ve trained a lot of neural networks over the years and I''ve come to find that the process isn''t nearly as simple as it seems. They are a leaky abstraction. Here''s what I''ve learned.\"\n\n**Tweet/X style (short-form):**\n- Pithy observations that compress insight\n- Strong statements (90% true, ignore counterexample police)\n- Unexpected connections between domains\n- Personal candor about struggles and discoveries\n\n### 2. Deep Technical Style (Opinion-Forward Analysis)\n\n**Use when:** Writing opinion-forward technical analysis about AI, LLMs, agents, or engineering topics. Best for content targeting senior engineers who want bold takes backed by evidence.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Contrarian, opinion-forward opening hooks\n- \"Do the simple thing first\" philosophy\n- Concrete examples with specific numbers\n- Takes clear positions and makes predictions\n- Varied sentence length, active voice\n\n**Load:** `references/deep-technical-style.md` for comprehensive guidance\n\n**Core Philosophy:** \"Do the simple thing first.\"\n\n- Embrace the black box: Focus on inputs/outputs, not internal mechanisms\n- Domain expertise over technical knowledge\n- Simplicity as virtue: Start simple, add complexity only when necessary\n- Opinion-forward: Take clear positions and make predictions boldly\n\n**Opening Hooks (choose one):**\n\n| Pattern | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Contrarian position | \"The death of prompt engineering has been greatly exaggerated.\" |\n| Practical pain point | \"So you need to hire someone to build your LLM multi-agent system...\" |\n| Challenge assumptions | \"If you''ve been stuffing thousands of tokens thinking ''more context = better''...\" |\n| Surprising simplicity | \"Claude Code isn''t built on a complex multi-agent swarm. It''s a single-threaded loop.\" |\n\n**Example opening:**\n> \"Most AI architectures are overengineered. A single-threaded loop often outperforms elaborate multi-agent orchestrations.\"\n\n### 3. LinkedIn Style\n\n**Use when:** Writing professional content for LinkedIn—thought leadership, announcements, industry insights.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Hook in first line (appears before \"see more\")\n- Short paragraphs (1-2 sentences each)\n- Line breaks between paragraphs for mobile readability\n- Personal angle or story\n- Call-to-action or question at the end\n- Strategic use of emojis (sparingly, professionally)\n- 1300 characters ideal, 3000 max\n\n**Structure:**\n\n```\n[Hook line that creates curiosity]\n\n[Personal context or story - 2-3 short paragraphs]\n\n[Key insight or lesson - bulleted if multiple points]\n\n[Call-to-action or engaging question]\n\n#relevanthashtags (3-5 max)\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n> Most AI features never make it to production.\n>\n> Not because the models aren''t good enough.\n>\n> Because teams build for demos, not for users.\n>\n> After shipping 50+ AI features, here''s what actually matters:\n>\n> → Start with the simplest possible implementation\n> → Measure what users do, not what they say\n> → Treat AI like any other code: test it, monitor it, iterate\n>\n> What''s the biggest lesson you''ve learned shipping AI?\n\n### 4. X/Twitter Style\n\n**Use when:** Writing for X/Twitter—quick insights, hot takes, thread explainers, engagement posts.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Punchy, high-signal first tweet\n- No filler words\n- Threads: numbered, each tweet standalone valuable\n- Contrarian takes perform well\n- Code snippets or visuals boost engagement\n- 280 characters per tweet, threads typically 5-15 tweets\n\n**Thread structure:**\n\n```\n1/ [Bold claim or hook]\n\n2/ [Context or \"here''s why\"]\n\n3-N/ [Key points, one per tweet]\n\nN+1/ [Takeaway or call-to-action]\n\n[Optional: link to longer content]\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n> Unpopular opinion: RAG is overengineered for most use cases.\n>\n> A well-crafted system prompt often outperforms a poorly designed RAG pipeline.\n>\n> Thread on when to use (and skip) RAG 🧵\n\n### 5. Simplified Technical Style\n\n**Use when:** Writing accessible technical content for broader audiences—explainers, introductions, \"what is X\" posts.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Start with the \"why it matters\" not the \"what it is\"\n- Analogies to familiar concepts\n- Avoid jargon or define it immediately\n- Progressive complexity (simple → detailed)\n- Concrete examples before abstract explanations\n\n**Example opening:**\n\n> Every time you ask ChatGPT a question, something interesting happens behind the scenes. The AI doesn''t just \"know\" the answer—it builds one, word by word, based on patterns it learned from millions of conversations.\n\n### 6. Tutorial Style\n\n**Use when:** Writing step-by-step guides, how-tos, implementation walkthroughs.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Clear prerequisites upfront\n- Numbered steps\n- Code blocks with comments\n- \"What you''ll learn\" summary\n- Troubleshooting section\n- Working example at the end\n\n**Structure:**\n\n```\n## What You''ll Build\n[One sentence + screenshot/diagram]\n\n## Prerequisites\n[Bulleted list]\n\n## Steps\n### Step 1: [Action verb]\n[Explanation + code]\n\n### Step 2: ...\n\n## Troubleshooting\n[Common issues + solutions]\n\n## Next Steps\n[Where to go from here]\n```\n\n### 7. Announcement Style\n\n**Use when:** Announcing features, releases, milestones, company news.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n\n- Lead with the news, not the backstory\n- What it is → Why it matters → How to use it\n- Keep it concise\n- Clear call-to-action\n- Links to more detailed content\n\n**Example:**\n\n> We just shipped streaming support for Deep Agent.\n>\n> Now you can see your agent''s thinking in real-time—tool calls, responses, everything—as it happens.\n>\n> Why it matters: Debugging agent loops is 10x easier when you can watch them run.\n>\n> Try it: `createDeepAgent({ model, onEvent: console.log })`\n\n## Writing Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Style\n\nAsk these questions:\n\n1. Where will this be published?\n2. Who is the primary audience?\n3. What action should readers take after reading?\n4. How much time will readers spend on this?\n\n### Step 2: Load Style Reference\n\nFor Deep Technical style, load `references/deep-technical-style.md` for detailed guidance including:\n\n- 7 opening hook patterns with examples\n- 5 argumentative structures\n- 10+ rhetorical techniques\n- 8 recurring themes to weave throughout\n- Sentence-level craft patterns\n- Pre-publication checklist\n\nFor other styles, refer to the characteristics above.\n\n### Step 3: Draft with Style Constraints\n\nApply the chosen style''s characteristics from the start. Don''t write generically then \"style\" it later—the style should inform structure, not just tone.\n\n### Step 4: Review Against Style Checklist\n\nEach style has implicit requirements. Before finalizing:\n\n**Karpathy Style:**\n\n- [ ] First-person, conversational voice?\n- [ ] Opens with personal experience or intriguing premise?\n- [ ] Honest about limitations (\"This might be wrong, but...\")?\n- [ ] Progressive complexity (simple → detailed)?\n- [ ] Contains dry wit or memorable lines?\n- [ ] Pragmatic advice, not theoretical?\n\n**Deep Technical Style:**\n\n- [ ] Contrarian or surprising opening?\n- [ ] Specific numbers/examples?\n- [ ] Clear position taken?\n- [ ] Explains \"why\" not just \"what\"?\n- [ ] Subheadings as mini-arguments?\n- [ ] Active voice throughout?\n\n**LinkedIn Style:**\n\n- [ ] Hook visible before \"see more\"?\n- [ ] Mobile-friendly spacing?\n- [ ] Personal angle included?\n- [ ] Ends with engagement prompt?\n\n**X/Twitter Style:**\n\n- [ ] First tweet standalone compelling?\n- [ ] Each tweet <280 chars?\n- [ ] No filler words?\n- [ ] Thread numbered clearly?\n\n## AI Slop Avoidance\n\n**Critical:** All content must avoid patterns that signal AI-generated text. Load `references/ai-slop-avoidance.md` for comprehensive guidance.\n\n### Quick Reference: Words to Ban\n\nNever use these overused AI words:\n\n| Category | Banned Words |\n|----------|--------------|\n| **Verbs** | delve, embark, unleash, harness, unlock, navigate, revolutionize, foster, elevate |\n| **Adjectives** | vibrant, bustling, intricate, pivotal, crucial, cutting-edge, robust, seamless, meticulous |\n| **Nouns** | tapestry, realm, landscape, paradigm, synergy, beacon, testament, game-changer |\n| **Phrases** | \"it''s important to note\", \"in today''s digital age\", \"dive into\", \"at its core\", \"a myriad of\" |\n\n### Quick Reference: Patterns to Avoid\n\n| Pattern | Problem | Fix |\n|---------|---------|-----|\n| **Em-dashes (—)** | Strong AI signal, ban entirely | Use commas, parentheses, periods (hyphens/en-dashes OK) |\n| Uniform sentences | All ~25-30 words | Mix 5-word punches with 40-word explanations |\n| Excessive hedging | \"might\", \"arguably\", \"perhaps\" | Take clear positions |\n| Immediate lists | Jump to bullets without narrative | Build tension first |\n| Perfect grammar | Zero typos feels robotic | Occasional imperfection is human |\n| Balanced both-sides | Artificial neutrality | Take a stance |\n\n### AI Slop Checklist (Apply to All Content)\n\n- [ ] Zero banned words from the list above?\n- [ ] **Zero em-dashes (—) in the entire piece?**\n- [ ] Sentence lengths vary dramatically (some <10 words, some >35)?\n- [ ] Contains specific names, numbers, dates?\n- [ ] Has personal voice or anecdotes?\n- [ ] Takes clear positions without excessive hedging?\n- [ ] Avoids \"In conclusion\" / \"To summarize\" closings?\n\n## Resources\n\n### references/\n\n- `karpathy-style.md` - Guide for writing in Andrej Karpathy''s conversational, pragmatic technical style with blog post patterns, tweet patterns, and recurring themes\n- `deep-technical-style.md` - Comprehensive guide for opinion-forward technical blog posts with detailed examples, rhetorical techniques, and pre-publication checklist\n- `ai-slop-avoidance.md` - Detailed guide to avoiding AI-generated content patterns\n\n## Extending This Skill\n\nTo add new writing styles:\n\n1. Analyze 5-10 examples of the target style\n2. Extract patterns: opening hooks, structure, tone, length constraints\n3. Create a reference file in `references/[style-name]-style.md`\n4. Add the style to the decision tree and Available Styles section\n5. Include a checklist for that style in the Review step\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:29:17.209Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Content Strategy Agents needing dynamic style adaptation across multiple platforms.","zh":"非常适合需要跨多个平台进行动态风格调整的内容策略代理。","ja":"複数のプラットフォームにわたる動的なスタイル適応を必要とするコンテンツ戦略エージェントに最適です。","ko":"다중 플랫폼에 걸친 동적 스타일 적용이 필요한 콘텐츠 전략 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Estrategia de Contenido que necesitan adaptación de estilo dinámica en múltiples plataformas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Stratégie de Contenu ayant besoin d''une adaptation de style dynamique sur plusieurs plateformes.","de":"Perfekt für Content-Strategie-Agents, die eine dynamische Stil-Anpassung auf mehreren Plattformen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Estratégia de Conteúdo que necessitam de adaptação de estilo dinâmico em várias plataformas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по стратегии контента, которым требуется динамическая адаптация стиля на нескольких платформах.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء استراتيجية المحتوى الذين يحتاجون إلى تعديل أسلوب ديناميكي عبر منصات متعددة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dynamically select and apply appropriate writing styles using Vercel''s AI SDK v6 framework, enabling consistent tone adaptation for technical blogs, social media content, and tutorial formats based on platform-specific requirements.","zh":"利用 Vercel 的 AI SDK v6 框架，使代理能够动态选择和应用适当的写作风格，从而根据特定平台的要求，为技术博客、社交媒体内容和教程格式实现一致的语调调整。","ja":"VercelのAI SDK v6フレームワークを使用して、エージェントが適切な書き方スタイルを動的に選択および適用できるようにし、プラットフォーム固有の要件に基づいて、技術ブログ、ソーシャルメディアコンテンツ、チュートリアル形式で一貫したトーン適応を可能にします。","ko":"Vercel의 AI SDK v6 프레임워크를 사용하여 에이전트가 적절한 작성 스타일을 동적으로 선택하고 적용할 수 있도록 하여, 플랫폼별 요구 사항에 따라 기술 블로그, 소셜 미디어 콘텐츠 및 튜토리얼 형식을 위한 일관된 어조 적용을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a seleccionar y aplicar dinámicamente estilos de escritura adecuados utilizando el framework de Vercel''s AI SDK v6, lo que permite una adaptación de tono coherente para blogs técnicos, contenido de redes sociales y formatos de tutoriales basados en requisitos específicos de la plataforma.","fr":"Permet aux agents de sélectionner et d''appliquer dynamiquement des styles d''écriture appropriés en utilisant le framework Vercel''s AI SDK v6, ce qui permet une adaptation de ton cohérente pour les blogs techniques, le contenu des réseaux sociaux et les formats de tutoriels basés sur les exigences spécifiques à la plateforme.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, geeignete Schreibstile dynamisch auszuwählen und anzuwenden, indem sie das Vercel''s AI SDK v6-Framework verwenden, was eine konsistente Tonanpassung für technische Blogs, soziale Medieninhalte und Tutorialformate ermöglicht, basierend auf plattformspezifischen Anforderungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a selecionar e aplicar dinamicamente estilos de escrita apropriados usando o framework Vercel''s AI SDK v6, permitindo adaptação de tom consistente para blogs técnicos, conteúdo de mídia social e formatos de tutorial com base em requisitos específicos de plataforma.","ru":"Позволяет агентам динамически выбирать и применять подходящие стили письма с использованием фреймворка Vercel''s AI SDK v6, обеспечивая последовательную адаптацию тона для технических блогов, контента социальных сетей и форматов уроков на основе требований конкретной платформы.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من اختيار وتطبيق أساليب الكتابة المناسبة بشكل ديناميكي باستخدام إطار Vercel''s AI SDK v6، مما يتيح تعديل النبرة المتسقة للمدونات الفنية والوسائط الاجتماعية وأنماط الدرس بالاعتماد على متطلبات منصة معينة."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating platform-optimized social media content for LinkedIn and X/Twitter","Creating deep technical blog posts with consistent tone","Producing tutorial content with structured learning pathways","Adapting writing style dynamically based on audience analysis"],"zh":["为 LinkedIn 和 X/Twitter 生成平台优化的社交媒体内容","创建具有一致语调的深度技术博客文章","生成具有结构化学习路径的教程内容","基于受众分析动态调整写作风格"],"ja":["LinkedInおよびX/Twitter向けのプラットフォーム最適化されたソーシャルメディアコンテンツの生成","一貫したトーンを持つ深い技術ブログ記事の作成","構造化された学習パスを持つチュートリアルコンテンツの制作","オーディエンス分析に基づいた書き方スタイルの動的適応"],"ko":["LinkedIn 및 X/Twitter용 플랫폼 최적화 소셜 미디어 콘텐츠 생성","일관된 어조를 가진 심층 기술 블로그 게시물 작성","구조화된 학습 경로가 있는 튜토리얼 콘텐츠 제작","청중 분석을 기반으로 한 작성 스타일 동적 적용"],"es":["Generar contenido de redes sociales optimizado para la plataforma para LinkedIn y X/Twitter","Crear publicaciones de blog técnicas profundas con tono coherente","Producir contenido de tutoriales con rutas de aprendizaje estructuradas","Adaptar el estilo de escritura dinámicamente en función del análisis de la audiencia"],"fr":["Générer du contenu de réseaux sociaux optimisé pour la plateforme pour LinkedIn et X/Twitter","Créer des billets de blog techniques approfondis avec un ton cohérent","Produire du contenu de tutoriels avec des parcours d''apprentissage structurés","Adapter le style d''écriture de manière dynamique en fonction de l''analyse de l''audience"],"de":["Plattform-optimierten sozialen Medieninhalt für LinkedIn und X/Twitter generieren","Tiefgehende technische Blog-Beiträge mit konsistentem Ton erstellen","Tutorial-Inhalte mit strukturierten Lernwegen produzieren","Schreibstil dynamisch basierend auf der Zielgruppenanalyse anpassen"],"pt":["Geração de conteúdo de mídia social otimizado para plataforma para LinkedIn e X/Twitter","Criação de posts de blog técnicos profundos com tom consistente","Produção de conteúdo de tutorial com caminhos de aprendizado estruturados","Adaptação do estilo de escrita dinamicamente com base na análise de audiência"],"ru":["Генерация контента социальных сетей, оптимизированного для платформы для LinkedIn и X/Twitter","Создание глубоких технических блог-постов с последовательным тоном","Производство контента уроков с структурированными путями обучения","Динамическая адаптация стиля письма на основе анализа аудитории"],"ar":["توليد محتوى وسائط اجتماعية محسّن لمنصة لينكد إن و إكس/تويتر","إنشاء منشورات مدونة تقنية متعمقة ذات نبرة متسقة","إنتاج محتوى درس مع مسارات تعلم منسقة","تعديل أسلوب الكتابة بشكل ديناميكي بالاعتماد على تحليل الجمهور"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vercel AI SDK v6 integration","Dependent on style selection framework accuracy","Platform-specific formatting constraints may apply"],"zh":["需要集成 Vercel AI SDK v6","依赖于风格选择框架的准确性","可能适用平台特定的格式约束"],"ja":["Vercel AI SDK v6の統合が必要","スタイル選択フレームワークの精度に依存","プラットフォーム固有のフォーマット制約が適用される場合あり"],"ko":["Vercel AI SDK v6 통합 필요","스타일 선택 프레임워크의 정확도에 의존","플랫폼별 형식 제약이 적용될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere integración con Vercel AI SDK v6","Dependiente de la precisión del marco de selección de estilos","Es posible que se apliquen restricciones de formato específicas de la plataforma"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec Vercel AI SDK v6","Dépend de la précision du cadre de sélection de styles","Des contraintes de formatage spécifiques à la plateforme peuvent s''appliquer"],"de":["Benötigt Vercel AI SDK v6-Integration","Abhängig von der Genauigkeit des Style-Auswahl-Frameworks","Plattformspezifische Formatierungsbeschränkungen können gelten"],"pt":["Requer integração com Vercel AI SDK v6","Depende da precisão do framework de seleção de estilo","Pode aplicar restrições de formatação específicas de plataforma"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Vercel AI SDK v6","Зависит от точности фреймворка выбора стиля","Может применять ограничения форматирования, специфичные для платформы"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع Vercel AI SDK v6","يعتمد على دقة إطار اختيار الأسلوب","يمكن أن يطبّق قيود تنسيق محددة بالمنصة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"879faed0bbb5770dc73f2027b7637b607fa0a7c70d0e8f6eef03f2435dd02941","qualityScore":37}');
