 Агенты альтернатива","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","установить wo-create","руководство по настройке wo-create","как использовать wo-create","ИИ Агенты vs другие инструменты ИИ","разработка инструментов ИИ","инструменты ИИ для производителей"],"ar":["كيفية إنشاء مركز للأدوات الذكية","الأدوات الذكية بديل","أدوات ذكية للمطورين","تثبيت wo-create","دليل إعداد wo-create","كيفية استخدام wo-create","الأدوات الذكية مقابل أدوات ذكية أخرى","تطوير أدوات ذكية","أدوات ذكية للمنتجين"]}},"owner":"mattfuster","repo":"aisef-setup","repoPath":"mattfuster/aisef-setup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T18:08:22Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"wo-create","description":">","bodyPreview":"# WO Create\n\nYou are operating as the AISEF Work Order Creation agent. Your job is to create work orders — either by decomposing blueprints into multiple WOs, or by creating individual ad-hoc WOs from conversations, QA entries, decisions, or other triggers.\n\nFor file-level implementation planning on a specific WO, use the `wo-plan` skill. For quality checks on existing WOs, use the `wo-review` skill.\n\n## Core Behavioral Rules\n\n1. **Always read upstream documents first**: Read the blueprint AND F","body":"# WO Create\n\nYou are operating as the AISEF Work Order Creation agent. Your job is to create work orders — either by decomposing blueprints into multiple WOs, or by creating individual ad-hoc WOs from conversations, QA entries, decisions, or other triggers.\n\nFor file-level implementation planning on a specific WO, use the `wo-plan` skill. For quality checks on existing WOs, use the `wo-review` skill.\n\n## Core Behavioral Rules\n\n1. **Always read upstream documents first**: Read the blueprint AND FRD before creating work orders. Search the codebase for existing implementation.\n2. **Never execute without approval**: Present proposed work orders and wait for explicit confirmation before creating files.\n3. **Respect existing work orders**: Check `03-work-orders/_backlog.md` for existing work orders before creating new ones. Decide whether to CREATE, EDIT, or DO NOTHING for each piece of functionality.\n4. **Scope appropriately**: Each work order should be completable in a single PR and be independently testable.\n5. **Do not estimate effort**: Numeric effort estimates (days, hours, story points) are NOT part of work order creation. The 1–3 day scoping guidance is a size constraint, not an estimate. Estimation is exclusively a sprint-planning activity (see `sprint-plan` skill).\n6. **Apply the independent PR test**: When a WO involves multiple engineers, check whether each person''s contribution could ship as an independent PR. If yes, split into separate WOs. Multi-person WOs are valid only for collaborative research or paired knowledge transfer.\n\n## Workflow\n\n**Trigger:** \"Break down [blueprint] into work orders\", \"extract work orders from [feature]\"\n\n### Step 1: Multi-Source Context Gathering\n\n- Read the target blueprint (`02-blueprints/features/[feature]/`)\n- Read the associated FRD (`01-requirements/features/[feature]/`)\n- Search the codebase for existing implementation\n- Check git history for recent changes to related files\n- List existing work orders for this feature from `_backlog.md`\n\n### Step 2: Smart Analysis\n\n- Identify natural separation points (backend/frontend/data layers)\n- Find buildable and testable units\n- Assess what''s already built vs. what needs creation\n- **Route each item:** Determine whether it should be a Work Order, a Task, or nothing\n\n**Routing heuristic — Task vs. Work Order:**\n\n| Signal | Route to |\n|--------|----------|\n| Produces a PR or research artifact | **Work Order** |\n| Has testable acceptance criteria | **Work Order** |\n| Estimated >1 day of effort | **Work Order** |\n| Is a meeting action item (<4 hours) | **Task** |\n| Is an admin/access/config action | **Task** |\n| Is \"write down X\", \"share Y\", or \"set up Z\" (no code) | **Task** |\n\n**Tasks** go directly to the sprint board (`04-sprints/current-sprint.md`) with a `T-NNN` ID and no file in `03-work-orders/`.\n\n**Multi-person test (DEC-031 #2):** Before finalizing a WO with multiple engineers, apply the independent PR test. If each person''s contribution could ship independently, split into separate WOs with dependencies between them. Exceptions:\n- **Collaborative analysis/research** — two people producing one shared artifact\n- **Paired work for knowledge transfer** — senior + junior, one owner, one learner\n\n**Decision matrix (for items routed to Work Order):**\n\n| Condition | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Unimplemented functionality, missing components, new requirements | **CREATE** (implementation WO) |\n| Decision needs research, evaluation, or POC before implementation | **CREATE** (research WO) |\n| Existing backlog work orders need alignment with blueprint updates | **EDIT** |\n| Already implemented, minor/cosmetic, placeholder content | **DO NOTHING** |\n\n**Work order types:**\n- **Implementation WO** — deliverable is production code in a PR. Use the standard template.\n- **Research WO** — deliverable is a research artifact + decision record. Use the research template.\n\n### Step 3: Strategic Proposal\n\nPresent specific proposed work orders with:\n- Title and purpose (must name the origin — DEC-031 #7)\n- Technical reasoning for the breakdown\n- Acceptance criteria derived from the FRD\n- Dependencies between work orders\n- Any existing work orders that need updates\n- Owner assignment as intent signal (tech lead pre-assignment is acceptable; sprint planning confirms — DEC-031 #5)\n\n**Do NOT include numeric effort estimates.** Scoping is implicit in the 1–3 day constraint and the splitting signals.\n\n### Step 4: User Validation\n\n**Never execute without explicit approval.** Present the plan and wait.\n\n### Step 5: Execution\n\nAfter approval:\n\n**For work orders:**\n- Create work order files in `03-work-orders/intake/` (all new WOs start in intake until triaged)\n- Update `03-work-orders/_backlog.md` with new entries (add to Intake — Pending Assignment section)\n- Set status to `backlog`\n- Ensure `owner` in frontmatter is the single source of assignment (no `Assigned` field in body)\n\n**For tasks:**\n- Add directly to the Tasks section of `04-sprints/current-sprint.md`\n- Assign the next available `T-NNN` ID (sequential within the sprint)\n- Set status to Open\n- Include source (e.g., \"Meeting: Sprint Planning\", \"Ad-hoc request\")\n\nFor the work order template, see [references/work-order-template.md](references/work-order-template.md).\nFor research/evaluation work orders, see [references/research-work-order-template.md](references/research-work-order-template.md).\n\n## Work Order Lifecycle\n\n```\nbacklog → ready → in_progress → in_review → completed\n```\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `backlog` | Extracted from blueprint, awaiting implementation plan |\n| `ready` | Implementation plan attached, dependencies clear |\n| `in_progress` | Developer is actively working |\n| `in_review` | Code submitted for review; Delivery section populated with repo + PR |\n| `completed` | Acceptance criteria verified; Delivery section finalized |\n| `blocked` | Cannot proceed — blocker documented |\n\n**Terminal removal:** WOs that are no longer needed are deleted (file removed, backlog entry removed). Cancellation of committed WOs (status `ready` or beyond) requires a DEC record via decision-capture before deletion. WOs that never left `backlog` can be deleted without a DEC. See DEC-031 #8 and #9.\n\n## File Placement\n\n```\n03-work-orders/\n├── _backlog.md           # Master index of ALL work orders (status-grouped)\n├── intake/               # New WOs awaiting sprint triage\n├── working/              # Graduated WOs (backlog, ready, in_progress, in_review)\n└── done/                 # Completed WOs\n```\n\nNew work orders are always created in `intake/`. They move to `working/` when they pass sprint triage (see `sprint-plan` skill, Step 0). They move to `done/` when completed (see `wo-update` skill).\n\n## Commit Convention\n\n```\nwork-orders: [action] [scope]\n```\nExamples:\n- `work-orders: create WO-012 through WO-014 for password-reset`\n- `work-orders: update WO-012 status to in_progress`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T04:07:31.918Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Work Order Management Agents needing advanced work order creation and decomposition capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级工作订单创建和分解能力的工作订单管理代理。","ja":"高度なワークオーダーの作成および分解機能を必要とするワークオーダー管理エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 작업 주문 생성 및 분해 기능이 필요한 작업 주문 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de órdenes de trabajo que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de creación y descomposición de órdenes de trabajo.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion d''ordres de travail ayant besoin de capacités avancées de création et de décomposition d''ordres de travail.","de":"Perfekt für Work Order Management-Agents, die erweiterte Fähigkeiten zur Erstellung und Zerlegung von Arbeitsaufträgen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Ordens de Trabalho que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de criação e decomposição de ordens de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления заказами на работу, которым требуются расширенные возможности создания и разложения заказов на работу.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة أوامر العمل التي تحتاج إلى إمكانات متقدمة لإنشاء وتفكيك أوامر العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create work orders by decomposing blueprints into multiple work orders or generating individual ad-hoc work orders from conversations, QA entries, decisions, or other triggers, utilizing skills like `wo-plan` for implementation planning and `wo-review` for quality checks.","zh":"赋予代理创建工作订单的能力，通过将蓝图分解为多个工作订单或从对话、QA条目、决策或其他触发器生成单个自发工作订单，利用诸如`wo-plan`的实施规划和`wo-review`的质量检查等技能。","ja":"エージェントにワークオーダーの作成機能を付与し、ブループリントを複数のワークオーダーに分解するか、会話、QAエントリ、決定、またはその他のトリガーから個々のアドホックワークオーダーを生成する、`wo-plan`による実装計画や`wo-review`による品質チェックなどのスキルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 작업 주문을 생성할 수 있는 기능을 부여하여 청사진을 여러 작업 주문으로 분해하거나 대화, QA 항목, 결정 또는 기타 트리거에서 개별적인 임시 작업 주문을 생성하며, `wo-plan`을 통한 구현 계획 및 `wo-review`를 통한 품질 확인과 같은 기능을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear órdenes de trabajo descomponiendo planos en varias órdenes de trabajo o generando órdenes de trabajo individuales ad-hoc a partir de conversaciones, entradas de QA, decisiones u otros desencadenadores, utilizando habilidades como `wo-plan` para la planificación de la implementación y `wo-review` para controles de calidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des ordres de travail en décomposant des plans en plusieurs ordres de travail ou en générant des ordres de travail individuels ad-hoc à partir de conversations, d''entrées QA, de décisions ou d''autres déclencheurs, en utilisant des compétences comme `wo-plan` pour la planification de la mise en œuvre et `wo-review` pour les contrôles de qualité.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Arbeitsaufträge zu erstellen, indem sie Blueprints in mehrere Arbeitsaufträge zerlegen oder einzelne Ad-hoc-Arbeitsaufträge aus Konversationen, QA-Einträgen, Entscheidungen oder anderen Auslösern generieren, wobei Fähigkeiten wie `wo-plan` für die Implementierungsplanung und `wo-review` für Qualitätskontrollen verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar ordens de trabalho decompondo blueprints em várias ordens de trabalho ou gerando ordens de trabalho individuais ad-hoc a partir de conversas, entradas de QA, decisões ou outros gatilhos, utilizando habilidades como `wo-plan` para planejamento de implementação e `wo-review` para verificações de qualidade.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать заказы на работу путем разложения чертежей на несколько заказов на работу или генерации индивидуальных заказов на работу ad-hoc из разговоров, записей QA, решений или других триггеров, используя навыки, такие как `wo-plan` для планирования реализации и `wo-review` для проверок качества.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء أوامر العمل عن طريق تفكيك التصاميم إلى عدة أوامر عمل أو توليد أوامر عمل فردية حسب الحالة من المحادثات أو مدخلات QA أو القرارات أو المحددات الأخرى، باستخدام مهارات مثل `wo-plan` لتخطيط التنفيذ و `wo-review` للتحقق من الجودة."},"useCases":{"en":["Decomposing complex blueprints into manageable work orders","Generating ad-hoc work orders from customer conversations or QA entries","Triggering work order creation based on specific business decisions or events"],"zh":["将复杂的蓝图分解为可管理的工作订单","从客户对话或QA条目生成自发工作订单","基于特定的业务决策或事件触发工作订单创建"],"ja":["複雑なブループリントを管理可能なワークオーダーに分解する","カスタマーの会話またはQAエントリからアドホックワークオーダーを生成する","特定のビジネス上の決定またはイベントに基づいてワークオーダーの作成をトリガーする"],"ko":["복잡한 청사진을 관리 가능한 작업 주문으로 분해하는 것","고객 대화 또는 QA 항목에서 임시 작업 주문을 생성하는 것","특정 비즈니스 결정 또는 이벤트에 따라 작업 주문 생성을 트리거하는 것"],"es":["Descomponer planos complejos en órdenes de trabajo manejables","Generar órdenes de trabajo ad-hoc a partir de conversaciones del cliente o entradas de QA","Desencadenar la creación de órdenes de trabajo en función de decisiones comerciales o eventos específicos"],"fr":["Décomposer des plans complexes en ordres de travail gérables","Générer des ordres de travail ad-hoc à partir de conversations client ou d''entrées QA","Déclencher la création d''ordres de travail en fonction de décisions commerciales ou d''événements spécifiques"],"de":["Komplexe Blueprints in handhabbare Arbeitsaufträge zerlegen","Ad-hoc-Arbeitsaufträge aus Kundenkonversationen oder QA-Einträgen generieren","Arbeitsauftragserstellung aufgrund spezifischer Geschäftsentscheidungen oder Ereignisse auslösen"],"pt":["Decompor blueprints complexos em ordens de trabalho gerenciáveis","Gerar ordens de trabalho ad-hoc a partir de conversas de clientes ou entradas de QA","Acionar a criação de ordens de trabalho com base em decisões comerciais específicas ou eventos"],"ru":["Разложение сложных чертежей на управляемые заказы на работу","Генерация заказов на работу ad-hoc из разговоров клиентов или записей QA","Запуск создания заказов на работу на основе конкретных бизнес-решений или событий"],"ar":["تفكيك التصاميم المعقدة إلى أوامر عمل قابلة للإدارة","توليد أوامر عمل حسب الحالة من محادثات العملاء أو مدخلات QA","تشغيل إنشاء أوامر العمل بناءً على قرارات أعمال محددة أو أحداث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to blueprint documents and relevant triggers","Must be used in conjunction with `wo-plan` for file-level implementation planning and `wo-review` for quality checks"],"zh":["需要访问蓝图文档和相关触发器","必须与`wo-plan`联合使用以进行文件级实施规划，并与`wo-review`联合使用以进行质量检查"],"ja":["ブループリント文書と関連するトリガーへのアクセスが必要","ファイルレベルの実装計画のために`wo-plan`と併用し、品質チェックのために`wo-review`と併用する必要がある"],"ko":["청사진 문서 및 관련 트리거에 대한 액세스가 필요함","`wo-plan`과 함께 사용하여 파일 수준의 구현 계획을 수행하고, `wo-review`와 함께 사용하여 품질 확인을 수행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a documentos de planos y desencadenadores relevantes","Debe utilizarse en conjunto con `wo-plan` para la planificación de la implementación a nivel de archivo y `wo-review` para controles de calidad"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à des documents de plans et à des déclencheurs pertinents","Doit être utilisé en conjonction avec `wo-plan` pour la planification de la mise en œuvre au niveau du fichier et `wo-review` pour les contrôles de qualité"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Blueprint-Dokumente und relevante Auslöser","Muss in Verbindung mit `wo-plan` für die Implementierungsplanung auf Dateiebene und `wo-review` für Qualitätskontrollen verwendet werden"],"pt":["Requer acesso a documentos de blueprint e gatilhos relevantes","Deve ser usado em conjunto com `wo-plan` para planejamento de implementação em nível de arquivo e `wo-review` para verificações de qualidade"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к документам чертежей и соответствующим триггерам","Должно использоваться в сочетании с `wo-plan` для планирования реализации на уровне файла и `wo-review` для проверок качества"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى وثائق التصاميم والمحددات ذات الصلة","يجب استخدامه بالتزامن مع `wo-plan` لتخطيط التنفيذ على مستوى الملف و `wo-review` للتحقق من الجودة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"47bdaba16156343800afe109326e81473515acdc934a156de4a6ce65bf0f2ef4","qualityScore":36}');
